/* =====================================================================
   THE VANISHING HOUR — every player's dossier, as they read it in "My file".
   Copied from the planning doc ("Dossiers" tab), with the host-only parts
   left out (At a glance, Host notes, Decisions for Jacob). Plain text with
   ## headings; js/dossier.js turns it into the confidential file.
   When a dossier changes in the doc, change it here too.
   Like story.js, this file holds secrets: keep it out of public view.
   ===================================================================== */
STORY.dossiers = STORY.dossiers || {};
STORY.dossiers["victor"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The fire (1972).** You were four when the Ashgrove warehouses burned. Your grandfather had let the insurance lapse to save money. By the end of the year your family had a famous name, a big empty house, and nothing else. You learned two lessons: never be poor again, and never be uninsured.\n\n**The climb (1990s).** In 1993 you and Hollis Grant founded Ashgrove \u0026 Grant, buying struggling companies and selling them off in pieces. You were the charm; Hollis did the math. By 1998 you were rich enough to start buying art, and you married Kendall Moore, whose family knew all the right people.\n\n**June (2000 to 2001).** In 2000 you met June Ellery, a 23-year-old art student who worked weekends at a gallery you visited. You bought one of her paintings. Then you started an affair. Early in 2001 she had your child.\n\nOn March 13, 2001, June came to your office in the city with the baby and asked for help. You had security walk her out, and you told your new assistant, Marlowe, never to put her calls through again. That night her car left Route 9 in the rain, and she died. The next morning you read about it in the Harbor Ledger. You tore the article in half. One half went into your desk; the other went into your pocket, and you have never thrown it away. You never asked what happened to the baby.\n\n**The long middle (2002 to 2021).** Ashgrove \u0026 Grant made a fortune, and the collection grew to 40 pieces. You divorced Kendall in 2009. In 2015 you forced Hollis out of the company, and Hollis has been suing you ever since. Years ago your old office papers, 2001 included, were boxed up and given to the museum\u0027s archive. You\u0027ve long since forgotten what\u0027s in them.\n\n**The fall (2022 to now).** Bad bets, a falling market, and a lifestyle that never shrank. Today the company is worth almost nothing, and the collection is the only valuable thing you own. You can\u0027t sell it without telling the world you\u0027re broke. So a month ago you raised the insurance by 40 percent, and you hired a crew to steal it.\n\n**Remy.** Last year you proposed to Remy Laurent. Remy believes you\u0027re as rich as you look.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** it\u0027s your gala. Officially, the Ashgrove Collection is on show for one night before it goes on tour. Really, it\u0027s the night it disappears.\n- **The plan:** the crew takes the art during the gala, the insurance pays out, and the enemies you invited take the blame.\n- **How you play it:** the perfect host until the theft, then the outraged victim demanding arrests.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Remy Laurent | Your fiancé(e). You love Remy, in your way. Remy can never find out the money is gone. |\n| Marlowe Pike | Your assistant since 2000. The only person who knows about June, and the only one you trust. |\n| Quincy Abernathy | Your lawyer of 30 years. Brought papers for you to sign tonight. |\n| Penn Calloway | Your money manager. Knows exactly how broke you are. Keep Penn away from the insurer. |\n| Sloane Archer | Your art handler for the past year, and secretly the crew\u0027s planner. You made the offer in a parking garage. |\n| Sterling Voss | The insurance appraiser, and the most dangerous person in the room. Charm them. |\n| Kendall Ashgrove-Moore | Your ex-spouse, married to you in 2001. Invited so the theft has a bitter ex to blame. |\n| Hollis Grant | Your old partner, now suing you. The perfect suspect. |\n| Lennox Blackwood, Indigo Hart, Wren Whitaker | Invited for one reason: so the police have someone to blame. |\n| Dominique Saint-Clair | Lent you the Winter Star for the night. The diamond gets the headlines while your art disappears. |\n| Rowan Hale | An FBI agent you\u0027ve never met. Something about Rowan\u0027s face bothers you, and you can\u0027t say why. |\n| Dusty Featherstone | A conspiracy podcaster. You\u0027ve never met. You had Marlowe add Dusty to the list, because loud is useful. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"The Winter Star is worth more than this building.\"\n- \"Hollis Grant has been suing me for eleven years. Some people can\u0027t let go.\"\n- \"Every piece in this collection is insured. I\u0027m not a fool.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, you raised the insurance a month ago.\n2. Yes, you were married to Kendall in 2001.\n3. Asked whether you have children, you say: \"None that I\u0027ve ever acknowledged.\"\n\n**Keep secret:** you hired the crew, you\u0027re broke, you invited your enemies to take the blame, and June.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **The theft is yours.** You hired the crew to steal your own art for the insurance. If it comes out, you go to prison, and Remy leaves.\n2. **June.** In 2001 you turned away a young mother and your own child, and she died that night. You\u0027ve carried half of the article about her death for 26 years.\n3. **You tipped off the press.** Two weeks ago you sent journalist Parker Lowell an anonymous message: \"Be at the Ashgrove gala. The Ashgrove Collection won\u0027t survive the night.\" Headlines make an insurance claim stick.\n4. **You had Marlowe add Dusty Featherstone to the guest list.** A conspiracy podcaster with a million followers, loudly blaming your enemies, is exactly the noise you want.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. Give the opening toast. At 0:50, tap your glass twice: the crew\u0027s signal.\n2. Before the theft, get at least three people suspecting one of your enemies.\n3. Keep Sterling Voss and Penn Calloway apart all night.\n4. After the theft, demand that the FBI arrest someone, and point them at Hollis.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Sloane Archer:** confirm the plan is still on.\n- **Sterling Voss:** charm the insurer and keep them away from the books.\n- **Quincy Abernathy:** go over the will you\u0027re about to draft, leaving everything to Remy.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **Half of a torn newspaper article** (the right half), folded in a sealed envelope in your inside jacket pocket. Don\u0027t open it. It\u0027s found on you after you die.\n- **Your toast card.**\n\n## Lying\n\nLike everyone, you may lie, except for your sworn facts. Lie freely about the theft, your money and 2001. You had nothing to do with the guard\u0027s death, and you\u0027re as shocked as anyone.\n\n## Your app\n\n**Bebbit**, like every guest: unlimited posts and look-ups, and every post carries your name. Tip: start rumors about your enemies early.\n\n## Costume\n\nBlack tie: a tuxedo, cufflinks, a white pocket square, and the most expensive-looking watch you can borrow.\n\n## Your last scene (about 1:20)\n\n1. When the theft is discovered, the empty spot where your painting should be holds a different painting: a young mother holding her baby, signed **J. Ellery**. You know exactly who painted it. Don\u0027t say so. Within a few minutes, tell someone you need some air, and go to the air spot (the host will show you where).\n2. Sloane Archer finds you first, worried that the lockdown has trapped the art inside. Talk it through. Sloane leaves.\n3. Rowan Hale arrives. Alone, he tells you the truth. You both get the lines on your phones. Let your face show the moment you finally understand.\n4. Rowan stabs you with Sloane\u0027s box cutter. With your last strength, write one word on a cocktail napkin: **JUNE**. If someone reaches you first, whisper it.\n5. Then you\u0027re dead. Once the room\u0027s attention moves on, slip out quietly. If you\u0027d like to keep playing, the host will give you any role that\u0027s still open.";
STORY.dossiers["rowan"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Your mother (2000 to 2001).** Your mother was June Ellery, a 23-year-old art student who painted at night and worked weekends at a gallery. You were born in February 2001. She never told anyone who your father was. In her diary she only ever called him **\"V.\"**\n\n**March 13, 2001.** When you were five weeks old, June took you into the city to see V and ask for help. That night, driving home on Route 9 in the rain, her car left the road. She died. You were found in the back seat, unhurt.\n\n**The Linden Street years (2001 to 2008).** Nobody came for you. You grew up in foster care, and the last house, on Linden Street, was the one you remember. An older girl there, **Vivienne**, called you \"Ro,\" taught you to pick the lock on the pantry, and let you follow her everywhere. You drew on everything, like your mother. When you were seven, Greg and Ellen Hale adopted you: a firefighter and a high school art teacher. They kept your first name and gave you theirs. You never saw Vivienne again.\n\n**The box (2019).** On your 18th birthday the state released what June left behind: a sketchbook, her diary, and one painting, *Mother and Child*, a self-portrait of June holding you, signed **J. Ellery**. The diary ends with one line: *\"Seeing V tomorrow. He\u0027ll help. He has to.\"*\n\n**The Bureau (2024 to now).** You joined the FBI at 23. You told everyone it was a calling. Really, you wanted access. For two years you dug quietly through records you had no reason to touch. In a local police log you found it: on March 13, 2001, Ashgrove \u0026 Grant security called the police to remove \"a woman with an infant\" from the building. Hours later, June was dead.\n\n**The proof (last spring).** You stood behind Victor Ashgrove at a charity auction and took the coffee cup he threw away. A private lab confirmed it: Victor is your father. He has no will, no wife and no other children. By law, everything he owns would come to you.\n\n**The plan (this winter).** You moved to the Art Crime Team, and you looked Victor up in FBI Headquarters. You found he\u0027s broke, that he raised his insurance by 40 percent, and that he\u0027s quietly paying a museum night guard named Charlie Pruitt. You understood: Victor is going to steal his own art. Then you heard he\u0027s engaged, and about to write a will leaving everything to Remy. You requested this assignment. You asked for Ellis Brooks as your partner, because Ellis trusts you completely.\n\n**The supplier.** When you found Victor\u0027s crew shopping for gear on NIGHTWIRE, you became their seller under a handle they\u0027ve never connected to you. You sold them everything they\u0027re carrying tonight, including a set of poison darts \"for emergencies.\" You kept one from the same batch. When Charlie dies, the dart will match the crew\u0027s perfectly.\n\n**Why.** June asked him for help once, with you in her arms, and he had her thrown out. You\u0027ve imagined this conversation every night for seven years. Tonight, Victor\u0027s art disappears and the insurance pays out, Victor dies before he can sign a will, and everything passes to the son he never asked about. And before he dies, he\u0027ll know who you are.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** officially, to protect the Winter Star. Really, to make sure Victor\u0027s theft succeeds, and that Victor doesn\u0027t survive it.\n- **The plan:** kill Charlie and frame the crew; leave your mother\u0027s painting where the stolen one hung; take Sloane\u0027s box cutter; kill Victor with it; steer the investigation to the crew.\n- **How you play it:** the best agent in the room. Helpful, sharp and calm. You\u0027re the one who \"keeps noticing\" evidence against the crew.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Your father. He doesn\u0027t know you exist. Watch him all night; let him catch your eye once. |\n| June Ellery (not a character) | Your mother. Never say her name out loud. |\n| Ellis Brooks | Your partner, and you chose him because he trusts you. Keep him close, and keep him busy. |\n| Dana Ward | Your boss. By the book. Dana makes the final arrest, so Dana is who you need to convince. |\n| Noor Haddad | The analyst running lookups. The most dangerous agent for you: if Noor looks you up, it\u0027s over. You\u0027ve noticed Noor has been messaging Victor, and you don\u0027t know why. |\n| Kit Locke | The evidence tech. Kit helped carry in your \"spare lighting case.\" Hope Kit doesn\u0027t remember it. |\n| Sloane Archer | The crew\u0027s planner, posing as Victor\u0027s art handler. Your fall guy, and the owner of the box cutter. |\n| Charlie Pruitt | The guard Victor paid to look away from the vault. He knows the theft is an inside job. If he talks, the insurance never pays. |\n| Vivienne Roux | The girl from Linden Street. You knew her the second you saw her. She hasn\u0027t placed you yet. Keep it that way. |\n| Parker Lowell | The journalist. Victor tipped Parker off; you sent a second tip, naming the enemies Victor invited. |\n| Remy Laurent | Victor\u0027s fiancé(e). If Victor drafts that will, Remy gets everything. |\n| Quincy Abernathy | Victor\u0027s lawyer, here to talk about the will. |\n| Marlowe Pike | Victor\u0027s assistant since 2000. In 2001 Marlowe was told never to put June\u0027s calls through. You\u0027ve never forgiven that. |\n| Dr. Ari Castellane | The curator. If anyone can read the signature on June\u0027s painting, it\u0027s Ari. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"I asked for this detail. The Ashgrove Collection is the biggest private collection in the state.\"\n- \"The crew will be inside already. They always are.\"\n- \"I was adopted. Good parents. Lucky.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent or Dana asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, you asked to be assigned to tonight\u0027s detail.\n2. Yes, you were adopted, at age seven.\n\n**Keep secret:** everything else. June, Victor, the DNA, the painting, Charlie, the box cutter, the tip to Parker, and Linden Street.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You are Victor\u0027s son.** Born Rowan Ellery. Proven by DNA.\n2. **You killed Charlie Pruitt** with a poison dart on the vault stairs, and made it look like the crew.\n3. **You killed Victor Ashgrove** with Sloane\u0027s box cutter, after telling him who you are.\n4. **You want the thieves to win.** The insurance payout goes to Victor\u0027s estate, which means to you.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Before 0:50:** kill Charlie and frame the crew.\n2. **During the theft:** make sure June\u0027s painting is left where Victor\u0027s painting was.\n3. **During Act II:** get Sloane\u0027s box cutter. \"Confiscate\" it in an interview, and don\u0027t log it.\n4. **Before midnight:** kill Victor before he drafts the will. Tell him the truth first.\n5. **All night:** help the art get out of the building without anyone noticing you helping.\n6. **At the vote:** get the wrong person arrested, ideally Sloane.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Ellis Brooks:** stay partnered. Ellis is your alibi.\n- **Sloane Archer:** get close in Act I, interview them in Act II, and leave with the box cutter.\n- **Victor Ashgrove:** one look across the room, early. Then wait.\n- **Avoid Vivienne Roux:** she knew you as \"Ro.\"\n\n## The cover kit\n\n### Your cover story, minute by minute\n\nThis is what you say happened. Memorize it.\n\n| Time | What you claim | What really happened |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 0:00 to 0:40 | Interviewing guests in the main hall with Ellis | True |\n| 0:40 | \"I heard something near the east hall and went to check. Nothing there.\" | You radioed Charlie to the vault stairs |\n| 0:45 | \"Still checking the east hall.\" | You killed Charlie on the vault stairs |\n| 0:50 | \"I was at the diamond arrest, at the back.\" | You arrived late. The arrest report doesn\u0027t list you. |\n| 0:55 | \"Securing the scene.\" | You left June\u0027s painting in place of the stolen one |\n| 1:00 to 1:10 | Interviewing, logging statements | True (and you took Sloane\u0027s box cutter) |\n| 1:15 | \"A perimeter sweep.\" | You were with Victor at the air spot |\n| 1:20 on | Investigating | True, and steering |\n\n### Safe truths (admit these freely; they make you look honest)\n\n- You asked for this assignment.\n- You were adopted at seven. Your birth mother died when you were a baby.\n- You looked Victor up before tonight: \"Standard vetting before a protection detail.\"\n- You radioed Charlie once, earlier, about a noise.\n\n### Never admit\n\n- June\u0027s name, or that you know who she was.\n- That Victor is your father, or the DNA test.\n- That the painting is yours, or that you\u0027ve ever seen it.\n- That you went down the vault stairs.\n- That you took Sloane\u0027s box cutter.\n- The tip to Parker.\n- Linden Street, or knowing Vivienne.\n\n### If they show you…\n\n| Evidence | Your answer |\n| --- | --- |\n| Clue 2 · your assignment request | \"Art crime is my unit. Of course I asked.\" |\n| Clue 5 · the radio log (you called Charlie) | \"I heard a noise and asked Charlie to check. I never went down there. That\u0027s when the crew must have got him.\" |\n| Clue 6 · the arrest report (you\u0027re not listed) | \"Dana wrote that report in a rush. I was at the back. Ask anyone.\" |\n| Clue 8 · the clipping about June | \"Sad story. Never heard of her.\" |\n| Clue 10 · your search on Victor, weeks ago | \"Vetting.\" If they point out the date is before you even asked for the detail: \"I was preparing to request it.\" |\n| Clue 11 · your personnel file names your mother | \"I never knew my birth mother. You think I\u0027m the only person whose mother was named June?\" |\n| Clue 12 · the sealed birth record | \"Adoption records are sealed. That\u0027s the law.\" |\n| June\u0027s painting, signed J. Ellery | \"Never seen it before.\" |\n| Sloane: \"An agent took my box cutter\" | \"I logged it at the command post.\" (You didn\u0027t.) \"Someone must have taken it from there.\" |\n| Vivienne thinks she knows you | \"I\u0027d remember you.\" Smile. Change the subject. |\n| Clue 14 · the DNA and heir papers | Your last retreat: \"Yes. He was my father. I came tonight to tell him, and I never got the chance. That makes me a son, not a killer.\" |\n\n### Phase by phase\n\n- **Arrival (0:00 to 0:15):** your briefing is with the FBI team. Be the most helpful agent there. Volunteer for interviews.\n- **Act I (0:15 to 0:40):** interview guests with Ellis. Plant one doubt about the crew: \"That art handler doesn\u0027t move like an art handler.\" Find Victor\u0027s eye once.\n- **The window (0:40 to 0:55):** leave Ellis \"to check a noise.\" Your phone will guide you through Charlie and the painting. Be back in the main room by 0:55.\n- **Lockdown (0:55 to 1:00):** stand next to Dana. Say early and loudly: \"This is the crew. They killed the guard.\"\n- **Act II (1:00 to 1:15):** interview Sloane and take the box cutter. Waste at least one FBI Headquarters lookup on someone harmless. If you take a statement that hurts you, log it badly or late. If the team starts decrypting the sealed birth record, offer to handle it yourself, and take your time.\n- **The second window (about 1:15):** when Sloane comes back from talking to Victor, it\u0027s your turn. Your phone will guide you.\n- **After (1:20 on):** you don\u0027t find the body. When it\u0027s found, connect the dots for everyone: Sloane was the last one with Victor, and it\u0027s Sloane\u0027s blade.\n- **Final push (1:45 on):** stay calm. If they\u0027ve caught you, use your last retreat line. Never confess. The vote decides.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **Your FBI credentials and a radio** (both props).\n- **The dart.** You kept it from the batch you sold the crew. Keep it hidden until 0:40.\n- **Your FBI case notepad.** Keep real-looking notes. You\u0027re the agent who writes everything down.\n- June\u0027s painting is handled by the host: you never have to carry it in front of anyone.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You\u0027re the only player who can lie about the murders.\n\n## Your app\n\n**FBI Headquarters**, shared with your team: about 10 lookups for the whole team, the statement log, and the case board. You can quietly misuse it: waste lookups, log statements late or incompletely, and steer what the team searches. Don\u0027t get caught doing it.\n\n## Costume\n\nA dark suit, white shirt, a plain dark tie, an FBI lanyard and an earpiece. Neat, forgettable, professional.";
STORY.dossiers["charlie"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Two jobs and a degree.** You\u0027re 21 and in your third year of college. You pay for it yourself: weekdays at a warehouse, nights at the museum, and homework on your breaks. You\u0027re tired all the time, and you\u0027re still the one who remembers everybody\u0027s name.\n\n**Your mom.** In September your mom, Denise, was diagnosed with cancer. Her insurance covers some of the treatment and none of the rest. You\u0027ve been picking up every extra shift there is, and it still isn\u0027t close.\n\n**The offer.** Three weeks ago a man you\u0027d only seen in the museum\u0027s donor photos stopped you in the parking lot. Victor Ashgrove. He knew about your mom. He said he needed one small thing: at 0:50 on gala night, stop watching the vault stairs for ten minutes. Two days later, $75,000 arrived through **NightBank**, a payment app on NIGHTWIRE that leaves no name, along with a note signed only **\"V.\"** You told yourself it was a donor being paranoid about his own art. You\u0027ve known better every day since.\n\n**Tonight.** You can\u0027t do it. Victor\u0027s art is about to disappear on your watch, and you\u0027re the guard who looked away. If it comes out, you lose both jobs, maybe your degree, and maybe your freedom. You\u0027ve decided to give the money back.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** it\u0027s your shift. You\u0027re posted on the east hall, which leads to the vault stairs.\n- **Your plan:** find Victor, return the money, and get out of the deal before 0:50.\n- **How you play it:** friendly and polite, and getting more nervous by the minute.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Bo Tate | Your best friend on the night shift. Bo has covered for you a hundred times. Bo doesn\u0027t know about the money. Yet. |\n| Victor Ashgrove | The man who bought you. You need to give him back his money tonight. |\n| Lane Garrity | Head of security, your boss. If Lane finds out, you\u0027re done. |\n| Jamie Ruiz | The bartender. Saves you food on every gala night. |\n| Harper Quill | The event manager. Always moving you around. |\n| Rowan Hale | An FBI agent. Before the doors opened, he asked you exactly where the vault stairs were. Strange question for someone guarding a diamond upstairs. |\n| Vivienne Roux | A guest you can\u0027t stop watching. Something about how she studies the diamond case. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Everyone\u0027s watching the diamond. Nobody watches the vault. The painting\u0027s still down there until the reveal.\"\n- \"One of the agents asked me where the vault stairs were before the doors even opened.\"\n- \"My mom\u0027s sick. I\u0027m working doubles.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Your post tonight is the east hall and the vault stairs.\n2. Asked if anyone has paid you, you say: \"Yes.\" You don\u0027t have to say who.\n\n**Keep secret:** Victor, the $75,000, the note signed \"V,\" and what you were supposed to do at 0:50.\n\n## Your secret\n\n**You took a bribe.** Victor paid you $75,000 through NightBank to look away from the vault stairs at 0:50. You\u0027ve spent some of it on your mom\u0027s treatment.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Before 0:30:** tell Bo, quietly: \"If anything happens to me, check my locker.\" (Your locker holds the NightBank receipt and the \"V\" note.)\n2. **Between 0:25 and 0:40:** find Victor and try to give the money back. He\u0027ll refuse. Let guests overhear some of it.\n3. **All night:** keep an eye on Vivienne Roux. She\u0027s up to something.\n4. **Tell at least two guests** that an agent asked you about the vault stairs.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Bo Tate:** the locker line.\n- **Victor Ashgrove:** the money.\n- **Jamie Ruiz:** your one friendly face. Get a drink of water, and tell Jamie you\u0027re in over your head.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A security radio and a guard\u0027s badge** (props).\n- **Your locker code: 417.** You always forget it, so it\u0027s scribbled in the margin of Bo\u0027s old shift schedule. The locker itself is set up by the host.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You had nothing to do with any theft, because you never got the chance.\n\n## Your app\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone: unlimited posts and lookups, and every post carries your name.\n\n## Costume\n\nA museum security uniform: dark trousers, a white or light-blue shirt, a dark tie and a radio on your belt.\n\n## Your last scene (about 0:40 to 1:00)\n\n1. At about 0:40 your radio (your phone will tell you) calls you down to the vault stairs: someone heard a noise. Answer out loud, so Bo can hear: **\"Copy, heading to the vault stairs. Wait, who is this?\"**\n2. Go down the stairs. Rowan Hale meets you there. He touches you with the dart.\n3. Fall, and stay down. The crew will pass you during the theft. Don\u0027t react.\n4. At about 1:00 Bo finds you. Stay still while the FBI processes the scene.\n5. When the host gives the signal, slip out.\n\n## After you die (optional)\n\nIf you want to keep playing, at about 1:30 you come back as **Reese Delgado, Sterling Voss\u0027s boss at the insurance company**. Reese got wind that a $115 million claim was opened within an hour of the theft, and is here to make sure Sterling doesn\u0027t mess this up. It\u0027s a smaller role with a few sharp facts, on a short separate card. It\u0027s your choice.";
STORY.dossiers["vivienne"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Linden Street (2004 to 2008).** You grew up in foster care. The house you remember is on Linden Street, where you were the oldest kid and the one in charge. There was a little boy who followed you everywhere and drew on everything. You taught him how to pick the pantry lock. Then one day a family came for him, and you never saw him again. There were a lot of kids, and you\u0027ve let most of them fade.\n\n**The Magpie (2015 to now).** At 18 you left with a bag and a talent: people believe you. You learned languages, manners and jewelry, and you spent a decade lifting stones from parties nobody thinks to guard properly. The police know \"the Magpie\" exists. They\u0027ve never had a face.\n\n**Dominique.** You hate Dominique Saint-Clair. Her family\u0027s foundation ran the foster care charity behind Linden Street, and while the Saint-Clairs posed for photos, the kids went without. You remember the year the heat was shut off. Two months ago you got yourself into Dominique\u0027s circle in Geneva as a charming new friend. Dominique thinks you\u0027re delightful.\n\n**The last job.** The Winter Star is the third-largest diamond in the country, and Dominique is lending it to Victor Ashgrove\u0027s gala for one night. One stone is enough to retire on at 30. Taking it from Dominique is the cherry on top. After tonight, the Magpie disappears for good.\n\n**The plan.** At 0:50 the Winter Star is lifted out of its case for the press photo. You know the alarm, the swap and the exit. You\u0027ve done harder with less.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** as Dominique\u0027s guest. Really, to take the Winter Star at the 0:50 photo moment.\n- **What actually happens:** the alarm goes off the second you touch it, and you\u0027re arrested. You don\u0027t make mistakes like that. Someone rigged it.\n- **How you play it:** before 0:50, the most charming guest in the room. After, a prisoner with information to trade.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Dominique Saint-Clair | Your \"friend.\" You despise her. Keep smiling. |\n| Frankie Doyle | You\u0027ve worked a job beside Frankie before. Tonight Frankie\u0027s dressed as catering. Professional courtesy: you stay out of each other\u0027s way. |\n| Blair Devereaux | Says she\u0027s a Devereaux buyer. There\u0027s no Devereaux family. You\u0027d know; you\u0027ve used the same trick. |\n| Lennox Blackwood | A rival collector who buys stolen art and asks no questions. A possible buyer, someday. |\n| Charlie Pruitt | The young guard who keeps watching you. Annoying, and sweet. |\n| Rowan Hale | An FBI agent. Every time you look at him, something pulls at you. |\n| Dana Ward | The lead agent. The one you\u0027ll have to bargain with. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely (before 0:50):**\n\n- \"Dominique and I go back years.\" (You don\u0027t.)\n- \"That diamond is the third-largest in the country. Imagine wearing it.\"\n\n**What you can trade (after 0:50):** you recognize people. Use it.\n\n- Frankie isn\u0027t really catering.\n- Blair isn\u0027t really a Devereaux.\n- Lennox buys stolen art.\n- Somebody rigged the alarm. It wasn\u0027t you.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. After your arrest: yes, you came for the Winter Star.\n2. Yes, you grew up in foster care.\n\n**Keep secret:** that you\u0027re the Magpie, which other jobs were yours, and (for as long as you can) everything you know about the others. It\u0027s your bargaining chip.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You\u0027re the Magpie,** and the police have been looking for you for ten years.\n2. **You hate Dominique,** and tonight was meant to settle it.\n3. **Linden Street.** You don\u0027t talk about it.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Act I:** stay in character as Dominique\u0027s friend, and get close to the Winter Star before 0:50.\n2. **0:50:** take the diamond. (You\u0027ll be caught. Make it a scene.)\n3. **In custody:** work out who rigged the alarm.\n4. **Bargain for your freedom.** Give the FBI something real, but not everything.\n5. **Figure out why Agent Hale feels so familiar.**\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Dominique Saint-Clair:** stay at her side until 0:50.\n- **Frankie Doyle:** a quiet nod. Agree to stay out of each other\u0027s way.\n- **After the arrest, Dana Ward:** your deal is with Dana.\n\n## Your memories\n\nDuring Act II your phone will give you three fragments, one at a time:\n\n1. A little boy who drew on every wall.\n2. The pantry lock.\n3. A name: \"Ro.\"\n\nYou\u0027re never sure. But the longer you look at Rowan Hale, the less you can shake the feeling. You decide whether and when to say it out loud.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **Gloves and a velvet pouch** (props), for the swap.\n- **A fake diamond** (a prop), for the swap that never happens.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You had nothing to do with the murders, and from custody you can prove it: you were in handcuffs for the second one.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**NIGHTWIRE**, on your own account (handle: magpie). You have just enough money for one file, to trade the FBI for your freedom. Anything more, someone else has to send you: you\u0027re the guests\u0027 and the FBI\u0027s way into NIGHTWIRE, if they\u0027ll pay. **Bebbit**, like every guest.\n\n## Costume\n\nThe best-dressed person in the room: evening gown or tuxedo, statement jewelry (fake), and gloves.";
STORY.dossiers["dana"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The rise.** At 27, you\u0027re the youngest agent ever to run an Art Crime detail, and half the Bureau thinks you got it too fast. Ambitious, fast and usually right. You\u0027ve recovered more stolen art than anyone in your unit, and you\u0027ve never once let anyone forget it.\n\n**The scandal.** Six months ago you announced the recovery of a stolen painting at a press conference. Two weeks later it was revealed as a forgery. The papers called it **\"the Ward Fake.\"** The journalist who broke the story was **Parker Lowell**, and Parker is on tonight\u0027s guest list. You\u0027re under internal review. Your boss was clear: one more mistake and you\u0027re out.\n\n**Tonight.** This is your last shot. Protect the Winter Star, catch anyone who tries for it, and walk out with a clean win. If something goes wrong, you need an arrest, fast, and it had better be the right one.\n\n**Your team.** You picked Ellis Brooks and Kit Locke. Rowan Hale requested the assignment himself, and you said yes, because he\u0027s the best agent you\u0027ve worked with. Noor Haddad was assigned by headquarters, and nobody told you why.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** to guard the Winter Star.\n- **Your plan:** a quiet night, a clean record, and your career back.\n- **How you play it:** in charge from the first minute. You make the announcements, you run the lockdown, and at the end you make the arrest.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Rowan Hale | Your best agent. Volunteered for tonight. You trust his instincts more than anyone\u0027s. |\n| Ellis Brooks | Steady and careful. Rowan\u0027s partner. |\n| Noor Haddad | Assigned by headquarters, with no explanation. Is Noor here to watch the diamond, or to watch you? |\n| Kit Locke | Your evidence tech. Meticulous. |\n| Parker Lowell | The journalist who wrote \"the Ward Fake.\" Keep Parker away from your investigation. |\n| Dominique Saint-Clair | Owns the Winter Star. If it\u0027s lost, so is your career. |\n| Victor Ashgrove | The host. Polished, and a little too eager to help. |\n| Lane Garrity | Head of museum security. You\u0027ll need Lane\u0027s cooperation for the lockdown. |\n| Vivienne Roux | After 0:50: your prisoner, and maybe your best source. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Intelligence says a jewel thief called the Magpie has been working this circuit. Stay sharp.\"\n- \"Nobody leaves this building without my say-so.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if another agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Rowan Hale requested this assignment, and asked for Ellis as his partner.\n2. Yes, you\u0027re under internal review.\n\n**Keep secret:** how close you are to being fired, and that you\u0027re terrified of a second \"Ward Fake.\"\n\n## Your secret\n\n**One more mistake and you\u0027re done.** You need a win so badly that you might take the first arrest offered to you. Someone in this room is counting on that.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Protect the Winter Star.** If someone tries for it, catch them.\n2. **Run the room.** Lockdown, announcements and the team\u0027s checklist each phase.\n3. **Work Vivienne\u0027s deal.** Decide what her information is worth, and whether she walks.\n4. **Recover the stolen art** before the night ends.\n5. **Make the right arrest.** After the vote, you arrest the person the room names. Make sure the evidence holds up, because you can\u0027t survive another fake.\n6. **Keep Parker Lowell from getting a story.**\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Rowan Hale:** your go-to agent. Get his read on everything.\n- **Lane Garrity:** coordinate the lockdown.\n- **Parker Lowell:** find out what Parker knows, and why Parker is really here.\n\n## Your powers (FBI Headquarters)\n\nShared with your team: about 10 lookups in total, the statement log, the case board, warrants to search a person or a bag, and detaining a suspect. You have the final say on how the team spends them. Only you can issue warrants (3 tonight) and detain. A warrant also lets you freeze that person\u0027s NightBank account, so they can\u0027t move money until you unfreeze it.\n\n## Your checklist\n\n- **Arrival (0:00):** brief the team. Assign Rowan and Ellis to interviews, Noor to lookups, and Kit to evidence.\n- **Act I:** walk the room. Meet Dominique, Victor and Lane.\n- **0:50:** make the arrest at the diamond. Take Vivienne into custody.\n- **Lockdown:** announce it. Nobody leaves.\n- **Act II:** interview Vivienne and decide on her deal. Assign the team.\n- **After 1:20:** announce Victor\u0027s death. Refocus the room.\n- **Final push:** review the case board with the team.\n- **Accusation:** call the vote, and make the arrest.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your sworn facts. You\u0027re not the killer.\n\n## Costume\n\nA dark pantsuit, an FBI lanyard and an earpiece. The most put-together person on the team.";
STORY.dossiers["ellis"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Eight years, by the book.** You\u0027re the agent other agents want reviewing their paperwork. Careful, patient and almost never wrong. You\u0027re not flashy, and you\u0027ve been passed over for promotion twice because of it.\n\n**Rowan saved your life.** Last year you and Rowan raided a warehouse full of stolen art. Someone knocked over a heater, and the place went up in minutes. You froze, and smoke filled the room. Rowan came back in for you and dragged you out. He burned his hand doing it, and still has the scar. The official report says you were injured in the fire. It doesn\u0027t say you froze. Rowan never told anyone. When Rowan asked for you as his partner tonight, you didn\u0027t hesitate.\n\n**What you want.** A transfer to the field office near your family. A clean, high-profile night like tonight would get it approved.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** Rowan asked for you.\n- **Your job:** interview guests with Rowan and log every statement in FBI Headquarters.\n- **How you play it:** calm, careful and friendly. You write everything down.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Rowan Hale | Your partner. He pulled you out of a fire. You\u0027d trust him with your life. |\n| Dana Ward | Your boss. Under pressure since \"the Ward Fake.\" You worry she\u0027ll rush. |\n| Noor Haddad | Quiet, and always typing. You\u0027ve noticed Noor messaging someone all night. |\n| Kit Locke | You and Kit unloaded the team\u0027s equipment cases together this afternoon. |\n| Victor Ashgrove | The host. Rowan keeps watching him. You don\u0027t know why. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Rowan\u0027s the best agent I\u0027ve ever worked with.\"\n- \"Every statement goes in the log. If you tell me something, it\u0027s on the record.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if another agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Rowan asked for you as his partner.\n2. Rowan left you at about 0:40, saying he\u0027d heard a noise.\n\n**Keep secret:** that you froze in the fire.\n\n## Your secret\n\n**You froze.** In the warehouse fire you froze, and Rowan is the only one who knows. You\u0027d be dead without him. It\u0027s why you\u0027ll want to believe him, and why doubting him will hurt.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Log every statement you take.** The statement log is how the whole room shares what people say.\n2. **Interview at least five guests,** including Vivienne after her arrest.\n3. **Keep track of where your partner is.** You\u0027re his alibi, and it\u0027s your name on the log too.\n4. **Decide, by the end, whether you still trust Rowan.** Nobody will tell you what to think.\n5. **Get the transfer.** End the night on the winning side of the case.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Rowan Hale:** your partner. Stay together.\n- **Kit Locke:** compare notes on the evidence.\n- **Vivienne Roux, after 0:50:** interview her.\n\n## What you might notice\n\nThis isn\u0027t scripted. These are things you\u0027ll actually see if you\u0027re paying attention:\n\n- Rowan leaves you at about 0:40 \"to check a noise,\" and isn\u0027t back until about 0:55.\n- Rowan\u0027s notes are usually perfect, but tonight some statements get logged late, or not at all.\n- Rowan disappears again at about 1:15, \"for a perimeter sweep.\"\n- Rowan once told you his parents were \"the only family he\u0027s ever had.\"\n\nNobody will tell you what to make of it. But during Act II, a guest who\u0027s been calling Rowan \"the sexy FBI agent\" all night may post on Bebbit asking where he disappeared to at 0:45. What you do with it is up to you.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your sworn facts. You\u0027re not the killer.\n\n## Costume\n\nA dark suit, an FBI lanyard and an earpiece. A notebook that never leaves your hand.";
STORY.dossiers["noor"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Counterintelligence.** You don\u0027t usually do art. You\u0027re a counterintelligence analyst, and for 18 months you\u0027ve been building one case, code-named **LARKSPUR**.\n\n**The case.** In 2019, Ashgrove \u0026 Grant bought Meridian Optics, a small defense contractor that made targeting sensors for the military. Victor shut the company down within a year. Its designs didn\u0027t disappear. They were sold through a shell company in Cyprus called Larkspur Holdings to a foreign buyer. That\u0027s fraud against the United States, and maybe much worse. Your first lead came from a whistleblower, **Wren Whitaker**.\n\n**Victor.** You don\u0027t want Victor; you want the buyer. For two months you\u0027ve been messaging Victor on a burner phone, offering leniency if he testifies. He\u0027s broke and scared, and last week he agreed to meet: tonight, after his toast. You deleted the messages, as protocol requires.\n\n**Why you\u0027re here.** Headquarters put you on the Art Crime detail as cover, so you could be in the building. Dana wasn\u0027t told why. Nobody on the team is cleared to know.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** officially, to run lookups for the team. Really, to meet Victor and turn him.\n- **The plan:** do your job well enough that nobody asks questions, then meet Victor in private.\n- **How you play it:** quiet, efficient, always typing.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Your witness, if he shows his nerve. Your whole case. |\n| Dana Ward | Your temporary boss, who suspects you\u0027re here to watch her. Let her think it. |\n| Rowan Hale | The agent who asks you for the most lookups. He\u0027s very interested in Victor. Why? |\n| Ellis Brooks | Kind and steady. Noticed you\u0027re on your phone a lot. |\n| Wren Whitaker | Your source. Don\u0027t let anyone see you two talk. |\n| Penn Calloway | Victor\u0027s money manager. Penn has to know where the Larkspur money went. |\n| Hollis Grant | Victor\u0027s ex-partner. Left before 2019, but may know how Victor works. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- Any lookup result the team asks for. You\u0027re the analyst, after all.\n- \"Headquarters assigned me. Ask them why.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if another agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Headquarters assigned you to this detail, not Dana.\n2. Asked whether you\u0027ve been in contact with Victor Ashgrove: yes.\n\n**Keep secret:** LARKSPUR, Meridian Optics, and why you were messaging Victor. You\u0027re not cleared to tell the team. You may decide to tell one person, if you believe the case is already lost.\n\n## Your secret\n\n**You\u0027re running a counterintelligence case against Victor.** If it leaks, the buyer disappears, and 18 months of work go with it.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Run the team\u0027s lookups** (about 10 for the whole team). Spend them well.\n2. **Meet Victor in private** after his toast, and get his yes.\n3. **Keep LARKSPUR secret** from the team, the guests and Parker Lowell.\n4. **After Victor dies:** save the case. Find his records before the night ends. His old company papers were given to the museum archive.\n5. **Find out why Rowan is so interested in Victor.**\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Victor Ashgrove:** the meeting.\n- **Wren Whitaker:** a quiet check-in.\n- **Penn Calloway:** where did the money go?\n\n## What you\u0027ll find\n\nIf you search the museum archive in Act II, you\u0027ll find Victor\u0027s 2001 office papers. The box is locked: Dr. Ari Castellane (the curator) has the key, and Wren knows which box it is. Inside, along with old Ashgrove \u0026 Grant files, is half of a torn newspaper article (the left half). It means nothing to your case. It might mean everything to someone else.\n\n## Your app\n\n**FBI Headquarters**, as the team\u0027s analyst. You run the lookups (about 10 for the whole team).\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your sworn facts. You\u0027re not the killer.\n\n## Costume\n\nA dark blazer, an FBI lanyard, a laptop or tablet, and a second phone you never explain.";
STORY.dossiers["kit"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The lab.** Eight years in toxicology at the state crime lab. You\u0027ve identified things that would make most people faint. You were very good, and nobody ever knew your name, because the detectives always took the credit.\n\n**The Bureau.** Two years ago you joined the FBI to be closer to the cases. Mostly you carry cases, bag evidence and fill in forms. Tonight you\u0027d like to be more than the person holding the bags.\n\n**This afternoon.** You and Ellis unloaded the team\u0027s equipment. The manifest listed **seven cases**. **Eight** came off the van. Rowan said the eighth was a spare lighting kit. You wrote \"8\" on the manifest and didn\u0027t think about it again.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** evidence and the case board.\n- **The plan:** a quiet night of nothing.\n- **How you play it:** precise, easily frustrated (people are always messing with your equipment), and quietly hungry for the credit you\u0027ve never had.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Dana Ward | Your boss. Under pressure. Wants answers faster than evidence comes. |\n| Ellis Brooks | Unloaded the van with you. Good company. |\n| Rowan Hale | Brought an extra case. Very helpful tonight. Maybe too helpful at crime scenes. |\n| Noor Haddad | New. Keeps to herself. |\n| Lane Garrity | Head of museum security. Knows the alarm system. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Evidence doesn\u0027t lie. People do.\"\n- What you find at the scenes, once you\u0027ve processed them.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if another agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. The team brought eight equipment cases tonight, not seven.\n2. The poison on the dart is not a tranquilizer.\n\n**Keep secret:** that you want the credit badly enough to hold a finding back until you can announce it yourself.\n\n## Your secret\n\n**You\u0027re tired of being invisible.** You\u0027d rather announce a breakthrough to the room than hand it to Dana first.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Process both crime scenes.** Post what you find to the case board.\n2. **Identify the poison on Charlie\u0027s dart.** It\u0027s lethal, not a tranquilizer, and the crew\u0027s own darts are all accounted for.\n3. **Prove the diamond alarm was tampered with,** and get the credit for it.\n4. **At Victor\u0027s scene,** identify the weapon. It\u0027s Sloane\u0027s box cutter.\n5. **If someone asks the right question** about the equipment cases, remember the eighth case.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Lane Garrity:** check the alarm together.\n- **Ellis Brooks:** compare what you both remember about unloading.\n- **The crew, once they\u0027re suspects:** count their darts.\n\n## Your app\n\n**FBI Headquarters:** the case board and the statement log, with your team.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your sworn facts. You\u0027re not the killer.\n\n## Costume\n\nAn FBI windbreaker or blazer, gloves, evidence bags and a clipboard.";
STORY.dossiers["sloane"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Coming up (2008 onward).** You, Frankie, Jules, Casey and Blair all came up in the same few years, working the same city. You found each other on small jobs and kept finding each other on bigger ones. You\u0027re the one who plans, and that\u0027s why they call you \"Blueprint.\" Between jobs, everyone goes their own way. When you call, they come.\n\n**Frankie\u0027s three years.** In 2017 a job went wrong and Frankie was caught. Frankie did three years in prison and never said a single name. Nobody on the crew has ever forgotten it.\n\n**The legitimate job.** A year ago you took a real job as an art handler for Victor Ashgrove\u0027s collection. Mostly it was cover and a way to learn the business from the inside. You packed, moved and installed every one of his pieces. You also asked a lot of questions about security. Victor noticed.\n\n**The offer.** Two months ago Victor met you in a parking garage. He knew exactly what you were. He wanted his own painting stolen at the gala, gone for good. He offered $2 million: $500,000 up front and $1.5 million on delivery, once his insurance paid out. The crew\u0027s job was to make the painting vanish and find a buyer at the party. You said yes in under a minute.\n\n**The last job.** You\u0027re 38. You\u0027ve been careful for 15 years, and careful is starting to feel like luck. This is the one you retire on.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** officially, to oversee the unveiling of the Ashgrove Collection. Really, to run the job.\n- **The plan:**\n    1. At 0:50 Victor taps his glass twice, and the whole room turns to the Winter Star photo.\n    2. Jules kills the cameras.\n    3. Frankie opens the vault.\n    4. You and Casey take the painting down from the vault and hide it.\n    5. Blair keeps the guests busy upstairs.\n- **How you play it:** quiet, professional, invisible. You\u0027re staff. Nobody looks at staff.\n\n## What really happens\n\n- **On the vault stairs you find Charlie,** the guard who brought you coffee during setup this morning, dead. Frankie and Casey want to call it in. Jules says no. **You decide: keep going.** It\u0027s your call, and it\u0027s final.\n- **The lockdown.** The building locks down before the painting can leave. It\u0027s hidden inside, and now you need a way out.\n- **Agent Hale.** In Act II, Agent Rowan Hale interviews you and takes your box cutter \"as a precaution.\"\n- **Victor.** When you go to tell Victor about the lockdown, he\u0027s in a side room, rattled and barely listening. You leave. A few minutes later he\u0027s found dead, stabbed with your box cutter.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Your client and your employer. He owes the crew $1.5 million. |\n| Frankie Doyle | Safecracker. Did three years and never gave you up. You\u0027d trust Frankie with anything. |\n| Jules Moreau | Tech. Runs NIGHTWIRE and the crew\u0027s chat. Still sore about Blair. |\n| Casey Brandt | Driver. Loyal, steady and the softest heart on the crew. |\n| Blair Devereaux | The face. Smooth and fearless. She and Jules used to be together, and it ended badly. Keep them apart. |\n| Charlie Pruitt | The young guard. Brought you coffee this morning. |\n| Rowan Hale | An FBI agent who seems very interested in you, and who took your box cutter. |\n| Lennox Blackwood | A collector who buys stolen art. He\u0027s sniffing around tonight. He doesn\u0027t know it\u0027s you. Keep it that way. |\n| Dr. Ari Castellane | The curator. You\u0027ve installed shows together all year. Ari trusts you. |\n| Marlowe Pike | Victor\u0027s assistant. Sees you at Victor\u0027s house all the time. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"I\u0027ve handled every piece in this collection. The painting in the vault is the best of them.\"\n- \"Nobody\u0027s touched the collection but me and the curator.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, you work for Victor, and you handled the painting this week.\n2. Asked whether an agent took anything from you tonight: yes. Agent Hale took your box cutter.\n\n**Keep secret:** the crew, the job, Victor\u0027s offer, the vault stairs, and Charlie.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You run the crew,** and Victor hired you to steal his own painting.\n2. **You stepped over Charlie\u0027s body** and kept going.\n3. **Victor is already a fraud.** In a year of handling his collection, you noticed some pieces were quietly replaced by copies. Victor has been secretly selling the real ones. The crew doesn\u0027t know.\n4. **You know what the painting is really worth.** Victor told you about the $115 million insurance claim, far more than the painting\u0027s real $81 million value. The crew has no idea, so their $2 million cut isn\u0027t the fair share they believe it is.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **At 0:50, run the job.** The painting comes out of the vault and goes into hiding.\n2. **Keep the crew together** after Charlie. Nobody calls it in.\n3. **After the lockdown, find Victor** and make sure the $1.5 million is still coming.\n4. **After Victor dies, sell the painting** to a guest through NightBank, for as much as you can. The crew\u0027s goal is $40 million.\n5. **Don\u0027t get arrested for Victor\u0027s murder.**\n6. **Find out who sold the crew those darts.** You think the seller, \"ashfall,\" is here tonight.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Victor Ashgrove:** before 0:50, confirm the plan. After the lockdown, find out what now.\n- **Blair Devereaux:** after Victor dies, work out which rich guest to sell to.\n- **Frankie Doyle:** your anchor. Check in after Charlie. Before 0:50, give Frankie your number for the vault dial: **61**. You learned it during a year of installing pieces in that vault. Only you know it.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A box cutter on your belt.** Wear it where people can see it all night. You\u0027re known for it.\n- **White cotton gloves** and an art handler\u0027s clipboard.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**NIGHTWIRE**, through the crew\u0027s wallet: buy data, and take payment through NightBank. **Bebbit**, like everyone.\n\n## Costume\n\nArt handler\u0027s blacks: black trousers and shirt, white gloves tucked in your belt, a visible box cutter and a lanyard reading \"COLLECTION STAFF.\"";
STORY.dossiers["frankie"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The tumbler.** You\u0027ve been opening locks since you were twelve. A tumbler is the part of a lock that clicks into place, and you can hear it click through a steel door. You came up with Sloane, Jules, Casey and Blair in the same few years. You talk too much and joke too much, everywhere except in front of a safe. There, you go completely quiet.\n\n**2017.** A jewelry store job went wrong. A city detective named **Lane Garrity** caught you with your hands inside the safe. You did three years. The prosecutors offered you a deal for names every month, and every month you said no. The crew has never forgotten it.\n\n**Geneva (2021).** Your first job out of prison went bad: alarms, guards, no way out. A woman at the party, a stranger, \"fainted\" in the middle of the ballroom, and in the chaos you walked out the front door. Later you learned her name: Vivienne Roux, the Magpie. You owe her, and you\u0027ve never had the chance to repay it.\n\n**Your son.** You have a son, Theo, who\u0027s 17. He\u0027s lived with your sister since you went to prison, and he barely knows you. He\u0027s tall, skinny and quick to laugh. After tonight you\u0027re going straight: one payday, then a chance to be his mom again.\n\n**The darts.** For this job you bought the crew\u0027s gear from a NIGHTWIRE seller called **\"ashfall,\"** including six darts sold as \"something to put a guard down quietly.\" You\u0027ve never used one. You don\u0027t plan to.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** catering. Really, to open the vault at 0:50.\n- **The plan:** serve, smile, chat, and at 0:50 slip downstairs with Sloane, Jules and Casey.\n- **How you play it:** the chatty server everyone likes. You make jokes about everything, especially when you\u0027re scared.\n\n## The vault dial\n\nAt 0:50 a steel dial opens on your phone in NIGHTWIRE. Turn it left, right, left. The combination is three numbers, and each one comes from someone else on the crew:\n\n1. **Number 1** is printed in the vault schematic file. The crew buys it on NIGHTWIRE.\n2. **Number 2** is Sloane\u0027s. She\u0027ll give it to you before 0:50.\n3. **Number 3** shows up on the vault-keypad camera when Jules loops the cameras at 0:48.\n\nCollect all three before you go downstairs. Without them you can still crack it by feel, one click at a time. It works, but it\u0027s slow, and every wrong full turn locks the dial for 30 seconds.\n\n## What really happens\n\n- **This morning** you joked with Charlie, the young guard, during setup. He laughed at all your bad jokes. He looked so much like Theo it hurt.\n- **At 0:50, on the vault stairs, he\u0027s dead.** You want to call it in. So does Casey. Sloane says no, and Sloane is the boss. You open the vault anyway, with your hands shaking for the first time in your life.\n- **After the job** you can\u0027t carry it alone. Somehow, quietly, you have to tell someone something.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Sloane Archer | The boss. You\u0027d follow her anywhere, or you would have, until tonight. |\n| Casey Brandt | Wanted to call it in too. Your ally. |\n| Jules Moreau | Brilliant, and cold about Charlie. It scared you. |\n| Blair Devereaux | The face. Wasn\u0027t there on the stairs. Doesn\u0027t know how bad it was. |\n| Vivienne Roux | The Magpie. She saved you in Geneva. She\u0027s here tonight, and she\u0027s going to get caught. |\n| Lane Garrity | The detective who put you away in 2017. Now head of security here. Lane cannot see your face. |\n| Charlie Pruitt | The guard who laughed at your jokes this morning. |\n| Jamie Ruiz | The head bartender. You\u0027re in and out of Jamie\u0027s bar all night with trays. |\n| Kit Locke | The FBI evidence tech. If anyone counts your darts, it\u0027s Kit. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- Gossip from the kitchen. Servers hear everything.\n- \"Try the crab cakes.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, you\u0027ve been to prison.\n2. If asked whether your darts are all accounted for: yes, all six.\n\n**Keep secret:** the crew, the vault, the darts, Charlie on the stairs, and Theo.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You opened the vault.**\n2. **You saw Charlie\u0027s body and didn\u0027t report it.** He looked like your son.\n3. **You have a son,** and everything tonight is for him.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **At 0:50, open the vault.** Get your three numbers first.\n2. **Stay away from Lane Garrity** all night.\n3. **Repay Vivienne** if you can. She saved you once.\n4. **After the job, tell one person outside the crew that Charlie was already dead when you got there,** without giving the crew away. Who, and how, is up to you.\n5. **Help sell the painting** after Victor dies. You still need the payday.\n6. **Find \"ashfall.\"** Whoever sold you those darts might be the person who killed Charlie.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Sloane Archer:** before 0:50, get number 2.\n- **Jules Moreau:** right after the camera loop, get number 3.\n- **Casey Brandt:** you two need to talk about Charlie.\n- **Vivienne Roux:** a nod before 0:50. After her arrest, find a way to help her.\n- **Avoid Lane Garrity.**\n\n## You carry\n\n- **The dart case** (six darts, all there).\n- **A catering tray and apron.**\n- **A lock pick set** in your apron pocket.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**NIGHTWIRE**, through the crew\u0027s wallet. That\u0027s where the vault dial opens at 0:50. **Bebbit**, like everyone.\n\n## Costume\n\nCatering blacks and a white apron, hair pulled back. A tray in your hand almost all night.";
STORY.dossiers["jules"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Static.** You came up with Sloane, Frankie, Casey and Blair. You\u0027re the one in the signal: cameras, alarms, phones and money. You\u0027re friendly, funny and easy to talk to. Underneath, you\u0027re the most ruthless person on the crew, and the others know it.\n\n**The warrant.** In 2022 a wire-transfer job in another state left your fingerprints in a federal database. There\u0027s a warrant with your real name on it. Any police ID check, anywhere, and you\u0027re done.\n\n**Blair.** You and Blair were together for three years. Then, after a job in Miami in 2019, Blair took the whole take and vanished. A year later Blair came back with half the money and an apology. Sloane made you keep working together. You\u0027ve never trusted Blair since.\n\n**The money.** You run the crew\u0027s NIGHTWIRE account and its NightBank wallet. Every dollar the crew spends or earns goes through you.\n\n**Jet.** Six months ago you took a job as pop star Jet Okonkwo\u0027s touring tech. It\u0027s the perfect cover, and Jet\u0027s booking tonight got you into the building. You run Jet\u0027s backing track for the 0:20 song from Jet\u0027s phone and a speaker. Jet is lip-syncing (damaged vocal cords); only you and Jet know. Jet trusts you completely and has no idea what you really do.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** officially, running Jet Okonkwo\u0027s performance. Really, the cameras, the chat, the wallet and the data.\n- **The plan:** at about 0:48, slip away from Jet\u0027s side and loop the building\u0027s cameras, so nothing is recorded from 0:50 to 1:00 while the crew takes the painting from the vault. Jet will notice you\u0027re gone.\n- **How you play it:** the cheerful tech who\u0027s everywhere and notices everything.\n\n## The camera loop\n\nAt 0:48 the security grid opens on your phone in NIGHTWIRE: six camera feeds and a 90-second timer. For each feed, splice in the recorded loop whose timestamp matches the live clock. Every wrong clip pushes the trace meter up, and so does time.\n\n- **If you pull it off,** the cameras show an empty building from 0:50 to 1:00. The vault-keypad feed also shows you **Frankie\u0027s third number** for the vault dial. Get it to Frankie fast.\n- **If you fail,** the cameras stay live, and somewhere there\u0027s footage of the crew in the vault. The FBI could find it.\n\n## What really happens\n\n- **On the vault stairs, Charlie is dead.** Frankie and Casey want to call it in. You say no, with a smile: \"Calling it in means police. Police means ID checks. We finish the job.\" Sloane agrees.\n- **After Victor dies,** the $1.5 million is gone. You run the sale: finding a buyer and getting the money through NightBank.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Sloane Archer | The boss. You trust her plans, not her feelings. |\n| Frankie Doyle | A legend for keeping quiet in prison. Falling apart tonight. Watch her. |\n| Casey Brandt | Too soft for this. Might talk. |\n| Blair Devereaux | Your ex. Took the Miami money. Never again. |\n| Jet Okonkwo | Your cover and your employer. Trusts you completely. |\n| Charlie Pruitt | The guard. Friendly. Unlucky. |\n| Harper Quill | The event manager, technically your boss tonight. |\n| Lane Garrity | Head of security. Owns the camera system you\u0027re about to switch off. |\n| Kit Locke | The FBI evidence tech. If Kit looks at the alarm or the cameras, Kit looks at you. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"The Wi-Fi password is on the bar.\"\n- Anything a tech would notice: who\u0027s on their phone, who keeps leaving the room.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, you had access to the building\u0027s camera system tonight.\n2. Yes, you know Blair Devereaux.\n\n**Keep secret:** the crew, the cameras, the wallet, the warrant, Charlie, Miami, and Jet\u0027s lip-sync.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You looped the cameras at 0:50.**\n2. **You told the crew to leave Charlie,** because one phone call means your warrant comes up.\n3. **You\u0027re wanted under your real name.**\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **At 0:48, loop the cameras** and pass Frankie the third number.\n2. **Keep the crew from calling it in.** Watch Frankie and Casey.\n3. **Never let anyone check your ID.**\n4. **After Victor dies, run the sale.** Find a rich buyer and beat $40 million.\n5. **Trace \"ashfall,\" the seller of those darts.** (See \"What you\u0027ll find.\")\n6. **Use your two hacked Bebbit posts** wisely.\n\n## Your powers\n\n- **The camera loop:** the cameras show nothing from 0:50 to 1:00, if you beat the timer.\n- **Two hacked Bebbit posts during the night.** Each one appears as if another real guest posted it, with one small tell that sharp players can spot.\n- **The crew wallet:** you hold the crew\u0027s NIGHTWIRE money.\n- **One unfreeze, once.** If the FBI or a court freezes a NightBank account, you can run an exploit from NIGHTWIRE that unfreezes it. You get exactly one use all night, so choose carefully.\n\n## The money\n\nNobody at the party has $40 million on hand. The rich guests have most of their money tied up, and freeing it takes an hour or more on the game clock. If you want a big buyer by the end of the night, the crew has to start working on them early.\n\n## What you\u0027ll find\n\nIf you spend money on NIGHTWIRE tracing \"ashfall,\" the trail ends at **a government network**. You don\u0027t believe it: no fed sells darts on the dark web. The crew is sure the seller is one of tonight\u0027s guests. Who you tell is up to you.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Sloane:** stay aligned.\n- **Frankie:** keep her from cracking, and get her the third number.\n- **Jet:** be there for the 0:20 song. Have a story ready for where you went at 0:48.\n- **The rich guests:** after Victor dies, scout your buyer.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A headset, a tablet and a lanyard** reading \"JET OKONKWO · TOUR CREW.\"\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**NIGHTWIRE**, as the crew\u0027s admin: the camera loop, the wallet and the unfreeze. **Bebbit**, like everyone, plus your two hacks.\n\n## Costume\n\nAll black, a headset around the neck, a tablet, and a roll of gaffer tape on the belt.";
STORY.dossiers["casey"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The kid.** You were 16, a runaway, and very bad at stealing cars. Sloane caught you trying to hot-wire hers. Instead of calling the police, she taught you to drive properly. You\u0027ve been with the crew ever since, always the youngest. They call you \"Clutch\" because you always come through when it matters.\n\n**Sloane.** You don\u0027t do this for the money. You do it because Sloane asked. She gave you a family when you didn\u0027t have one. If Sloane says go, you go.\n\n**The rule.** In fifteen years the crew has had one rule: nobody gets hurt. You\u0027re a thief, not a killer. You\u0027ve never seen a dead body in your life.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** driving the catering van. Really, the getaway.\n- **The plan:** at 0:50, help Sloane carry the painting from the vault and hide it, then drive it out at the end of the night.\n- **How you play it:** busy, helpful and a little jumpy.\n\n## What really happens\n\n- **On the vault stairs, you see your first dead body.** It\u0027s Charlie, the guard who held the loading door for you this morning. You want to call it in. Frankie does too. Sloane says no. You do what Sloane says. You always have.\n- **Then the lockdown.** The painting is hidden inside, the van is trapped, and getting it out is now your job alone. The rest of the crew works on finding a buyer.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Sloane Archer | Family. She took you in at 16. You\u0027d do anything for her, even this. |\n| Frankie Doyle | Wanted to call it in, like you. The two of you understand each other tonight. |\n| Jules Moreau | Smiled when they said \"leave him.\" It scared you. |\n| Blair Devereaux | Like a big sister. She wasn\u0027t on the stairs, and you\u0027re not sure how to tell her. |\n| Charlie Pruitt | Held the loading door for you this morning. Now he\u0027s the first dead person you\u0027ve ever seen. |\n| Jamie Ruiz | The head bartender. You share the back room all night. A friend. |\n| Harper Quill | The event manager. Harper decides what leaves the building and when. |\n| Lane Garrity | Head of security. Runs the lockdown. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"The loading dock\u0027s been busy all night.\"\n- Kitchen gossip, through Jamie.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, you drove the catering van here tonight.\n2. If asked whether you\u0027ve ever hurt anyone: \"Never. Not once.\"\n\n**Keep secret:** the crew, the vault, the painting\u0027s hiding place, and Charlie on the stairs.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You helped take the painting.**\n2. **You saw Charlie\u0027s body** and said nothing, because Sloane said so.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **At 0:50, help take the painting** from the vault and hide it.\n2. **After the lockdown, get the painting out.** Find a way: talk Harper or Lane into clearing the catering van at the end of the night, or find another route.\n3. **Keep Frankie steady.** You\u0027re both shaking.\n4. **Tell Blair what happened on the stairs.**\n5. **Don\u0027t let anyone search the van.**\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Harper Quill:** clearance for the van.\n- **Jamie Ruiz:** your friend. You might need to talk.\n- **Frankie Doyle:** check in after the stairs.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **The catering van keys** and a delivery clipboard.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**NIGHTWIRE**, through the crew\u0027s chat. **Bebbit**, like everyone. If you want a break from the stairs, the crew can play the casino from NIGHTWIRE.\n\n## Costume\n\nCatering company polo or black work shirt, a cap, and the van keys on a lanyard.";
STORY.dossiers["blair"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Velvet.** You came up with Sloane, Frankie, Jules and Casey. You were always the face: the one who talks her way through the front door so everyone else can come in the back. They call you \"Velvet\" because nobody ever feels you coming.\n\n**There is no Devereaux family.** You invented them for this job, down to a fake website and a shipping company in Marseille. It will hold up to a polite question. It won\u0027t hold up to a determined one.\n\n**Miami (2019).** After the Miami job, a man the crew had crossed found out who all of you were. He gave you a choice: pay him everything, or he\u0027d hand the whole crew to the police. You paid him the full take. You couldn\u0027t explain without putting everyone in danger, so you disappeared for a year to draw the heat away. When you came back, you returned half the money (everything you could earn back) and an apology. You\u0027ve never told anyone the truth. Jules thinks you\u0027re a thief who stole from your own family. You let Jules think it.\n\n**Jules.** You were together for three years. You never stopped caring. Jules never forgave you.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** as a rich new collector. Really, to keep the guests\u0027 attention wherever the crew needs it.\n- **The plan:** work the rich guests all of Act I. At 0:50, keep the room facing the Winter Star.\n- **How you play it:** glamorous, generous and impossible to say no to.\n\n## What really happens\n\n- **You weren\u0027t on the stairs.** Later, Casey tells you about Charlie, and that Sloane decided to leave him. Sloane didn\u0027t tell you herself. You\u0027re furious.\n- **After Victor dies,** the crew\u0027s last $1.5 million is gone. The fake buyer has to find a real one. You\u0027re the crew\u0027s salesperson now.\n\n## The money\n\nNobody at the party has $40 million on hand. The rich guests keep most of their money tied up in investments. Each of them can free it up once tonight, and it takes an hour or more on the game clock to clear. So the sale really starts in Act I: find out who has money, and get them to start freeing it up early, before they know why.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Sloane Archer | The boss. She hid Charlie from you. You need to have that out with her. |\n| Jules Moreau | Your ex. Thinks you\u0027re a thief. You know better, and you can\u0027t say. |\n| Frankie Doyle | Falling apart over Charlie. You\u0027d like to help her. |\n| Casey Brandt | Like a little sister. She told you the truth when Sloane didn\u0027t. |\n| Vivienne Roux | Another con artist. You spotted each other in seconds. You have a standoff: neither exposes the other. Then she gets arrested. Will she trade your name? |\n| Drew Kincaid | Tech billionaire. Shopping for art and influence. A buyer. |\n| Ainsley Vandermeer | Old-money heir. Bored and rich. A buyer, but old money moves slowly. |\n| Cameron Thorne | Investor. Here to collect money from Victor. Might want art instead. |\n| Lennox Blackwood | Buys stolen art, and he\u0027s here to buy tonight. After Vivienne names him, the FBI will be watching him. Too dangerous. |\n| Parker Lowell | A journalist. One web search away from finding out the Devereaux family doesn\u0027t exist. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"My family ships half of Europe\u0027s wine. I\u0027d like to own something beautiful for once.\"\n- Gossip from the rich guests. They tell you everything.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether Devereaux is your real name: \"No.\"\n2. Asked whether you were near the vault at 0:50: \"No.\" (True: you were upstairs.)\n\n**Keep secret:** the crew, the job, your real name, and Miami.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You\u0027re not a Devereaux.** The family doesn\u0027t exist.\n2. **You\u0027re part of the crew.**\n3. **The truth about Miami.** You saved the crew, and you\u0027ve never told them.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Act I:** win over at least three rich guests. Find out which of them has money, nerve and no questions, and get them freeing up money early.\n2. **At 0:50:** keep the room watching the diamond.\n3. **After you hear about Charlie:** confront Sloane, privately.\n4. **After Victor dies:** sell the painting to one of the rich guests through NightBank, for as much as you can. The crew\u0027s goal is $40 million.\n5. **Keep your cover:** nobody checks your real name.\n6. **Watch Vivienne.** If she starts trading names, yours could be next.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Drew Kincaid, Ainsley Vandermeer and Cameron Thorne:** your buyers.\n- **Vivienne Roux:** the standoff, before 0:50.\n- **Sloane:** after Casey tells you.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **Business cards** for \"Devereaux Maritime, Marseille.\"\n- **A champagne glass** you never actually drink from.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**NIGHTWIRE**, through the crew\u0027s chat, for the sale. **Bebbit**, like everyone. The casino is a good place to meet rich guests: the crew can play from NIGHTWIRE.\n\n## Costume\n\nThe second-best-dressed person in the room (Vivienne is the first, and you both know it): a gown or tuxedo, and old-money jewelry.";
STORY.dossiers["lane"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Twenty years on the job.** You were a good detective: patient, stubborn and hard to fool. In 2017 you caught a safecracker red-handed, hands inside a jewelry store safe. The safecracker did three years and never named a single partner. You\u0027ve always respected that, a little.\n\n**Private security.** Three years ago you left the police for one simple reason: private security pays better. The museum hired you to run its guards, and you\u0027ve made it the tightest building in the city.\n\n**Charlie.** Charlie Pruitt has worked nights for you for two years. Hardworking, polite, never complains, always studying on his breaks. You\u0027d never say it out loud, but he\u0027s your favorite.\n\n**This week.** Two things happened that you keep turning over:\n\n- **Charlie asked for the vault stairs.** He always takes the lobby desk, where it\u0027s quiet enough to study. This week he asked, specifically, for the east hall and the vault stairs on gala night. You approved it. You meant to ask him why.\n- **The alarm code.** During setup this afternoon, one of the FBI agents asked for the diamond case\u0027s alarm panel code \"for FBI protocol.\" You gave it. It\u0027s what you\u0027d do for any federal detail.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** it\u0027s your building.\n- **Your job:** guards, doors, cameras and, if it comes to that, the lockdown.\n- **How you play it:** calm, watchful, and the last person anyone should try to lie to.\n\n## What really happens\n\n- **At 0:50 the alarm screams** at the Winter Star. The FBI arrests a guest.\n- **Charlie stops answering his radio.** Bo goes to check.\n- **Charlie is dead on the stairs you put him on.**\n- **You and Dana lock the building down.** Nobody leaves without your say-so.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Charlie Pruitt | Your favorite guard. You put him on the vault stairs. |\n| Bo Tate | Charlie\u0027s best friend on the night shift. Steady. Keep Bo close tonight. |\n| Dana Ward | The FBI lead. Young, under pressure. You\u0027ll run the lockdown together. |\n| Kit Locke | The FBI evidence tech. You\u0027ll check the alarm together. |\n| Rowan Hale | An FBI agent. Friendly, very interested in the building\u0027s layout. |\n| Harper Quill | The event manager. Fights you over every closed door. |\n| Victor Ashgrove | The donor. He insisted the painting stay in the vault until its reveal. You thought it was vanity. |\n| A catering server | Something about one of the servers\u0027 faces bothers you. You can\u0027t place it. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"This is the tightest building in the city.\"\n- \"Victor insisted the painting stay in the vault until the reveal.\"\n- \"Charlie never asked for anything. This week, he asked for the vault stairs.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, you approved Charlie\u0027s request to work the vault stairs tonight.\n2. Yes, you gave the diamond case\u0027s alarm code to the FBI during setup.\n\n**Keep secret:** that you never asked Charlie why, and that you gave the code away without a second thought.\n\n## Your secret\n\n**You put Charlie on those stairs,** and you never asked him why he wanted them. If you had, he might be alive.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Run a clean night.** Guards on post, doors watched.\n2. **After the alarm, work out how it went off.** With Kit, check whether it was tampered with. Only a few people had that code.\n3. **Run the lockdown** with Dana. Decide what, and who, can leave at the end of the night. The right story might change your mind.\n4. **Find out why Charlie wanted the vault stairs.**\n5. **Place that catering server\u0027s face.**\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Bo Tate:** after Charlie, look after Bo.\n- **Kit Locke:** the alarm.\n- **Dana Ward:** the lockdown.\n\n## Recognizing Frankie\n\nFrankie Doyle, the crew\u0027s safecracker, is working tonight disguised as a catering server. You arrested Frankie in 2017. During Act I your phone tells you only that a server\u0027s face is familiar. If you come face to face with Frankie after the lockdown, your phone tells you who it is. What you do then is up to you.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A security radio, a keycard and a lanyard.**\n- **Your security binder.** Tonight\u0027s radio log is in it, every call with its time. It\u0027s a paper clue. Who you show it to is up to you.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your own account. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nA dark suit and an earpiece. Looks like a detective, because Lane was one.";
STORY.dossiers["bo"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Fifteen years of nights.** You\u0027ve walked these halls longer than anyone. It\u0027s quiet work, and you like it that way.\n\n**Charlie.** When Charlie Pruitt started two years ago, he was 19, exhausted and trying to do everything at once. You took him under your wing. You traded him the easy shifts when he had exams, brought him dinner, and told him to sleep. It always bothered you that a kid like that had to work nights at all. He\u0027d laugh and say, \"Somebody has to pay for college, Bo.\" You never knew how bad things were with his mom. He never told anyone.\n\n**This morning.** Charlie pulled you aside and said, quietly: **\"If anything happens to me, check my locker.\"** He laughed it off. You didn\u0027t.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** your shift. You\u0027re posted near the main hall, by the Winter Star, and you stay there all night, radio on.\n- **Your job:** watch the floor, watch the radio, watch out for Charlie.\n- **How you play it:** warm and steady, the guard everyone trusts. Then, after 1:00, a person holding it together.\n\n## What really happens\n\n- **At about 0:40, on the radio,** you hear Charlie say: **\"Copy, heading to the vault stairs. Wait, who is this?\"** Then nothing.\n- **At 0:50 the diamond alarm goes off,** and the whole room is chaos.\n- **Charlie doesn\u0027t answer his radio.** At about 1:00, you go to check.\n- **You find him on the vault stairs.** There\u0027s a small dart on the step beside him. Don\u0027t touch it. Get the FBI.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Charlie Pruitt | The kid you looked out for. |\n| Lane Garrity | Your boss. Fair. Lane put Charlie on the vault stairs tonight. |\n| Jamie Ruiz | The bartender. Saved food for Charlie every gala night. |\n| Harper Quill | The event manager. Always rushing. |\n| Victor Ashgrove | The rich donor. You saw him and Charlie arguing in Act I. |\n| Dana Ward | The FBI lead. Wants answers fast. You want the right ones. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Charlie was the best kid in this building.\"\n- \"I heard his last radio call. Somebody else was on that channel.\"\n- \"He was working two jobs and going to school. He never complained once.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. You heard Charlie\u0027s last radio call, word for word.\n2. Asked whether Charlie told you anything before tonight: yes. \"If anything happens to me, check my locker.\"\n\n**Keep secret:** what\u0027s in the locker, until you decide what to do with it.\n\n## Your secret\n\n**The locker.** Charlie\u0027s locker (number 12) has a three-digit lock. Inside is a NightBank receipt for $75,000 and a note on Victor Ashgrove\u0027s stationery, signed only \"V.\" Charlie took a bribe. You have to decide: protect his name, or use it to find his killer.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Find out who killed Charlie,** no matter whose side that puts you on.\n2. **Open Charlie\u0027s locker** after you find him, and decide what to do with what\u0027s inside.\n3. **Work out who was on the radio** when Charlie said \"Who is this?\"\n4. **Look after Charlie\u0027s memory.** Make sure the room knows who he was.\n5. **Decide who you blame first.** That\u0027s up to you.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Lane Garrity:** why was Charlie on those stairs?\n- **Jamie Ruiz:** Charlie talked to Jamie. What did he say tonight?\n- **Victor Ashgrove:** what were you two arguing about?\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A security radio, a flashlight and a guard\u0027s badge.**\n- **An old shift schedule.** Charlie always forgot his locker combination, so he wrote it in the margin. Look closely.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your own account. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nThe museum security uniform: dark trousers, a light shirt, a dark tie, and a radio on the belt.";
STORY.dossiers["harper"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The planner.** At 29, you\u0027re the youngest senior event manager at your company. You write everything down: every change, every request, and who asked for it. Your planner is your brain.\n\n**The gamble.** Victor Ashgrove\u0027s gala is the biggest event you\u0027ve ever run. The company normally takes the full payment up front. Victor asked for \"a few weeks\u0027 grace,\" and you vouched for him personally. The invoice is **$180,000**, and he hasn\u0027t paid a cent. If your boss finds out, you\u0027re fired. You\u0027ve been telling your boss the money is \"in transit\" for three weeks.\n\n**Parker.** The journalist Parker Lowell promised you a glowing write-up of tonight. In return, you\u0027ve been passing along the occasional detail: the guest list, the schedule, a little gossip.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** it\u0027s your event.\n- **Your job:** keep the night on schedule, keep Victor happy, and get paid.\n- **How you play it:** everywhere at once, clipboard first, slightly panicking.\n\n## What really happens\n\n- **At 0:50 you run the Winter Star photo moment.** The diamond is lifted from its case for the press, and the alarm goes off the second someone touches it.\n- **Then Charlie is found dead, and the building locks down.** Your perfect schedule is gone.\n- **When Victor dies, so does your $180,000.**\n\n## The casino\n\nTonight\u0027s charity casino, the Saint-Clair Foundation Casino, runs inside NightBank. The house always wins in the end, and its winnings go to Dominique Saint-Clair\u0027s foundation. Your company takes **10% of the house\u0027s take** as the event fee, paid straight into your NightBank account as the night goes on. It won\u0027t cover $180,000 by itself. The more people play, though, the closer you get. Talk the casino up.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Your client. Charming, demanding, and $180,000 behind. |\n| Lane Garrity | Head of security. Keeps closing doors you need open. |\n| Jamie Ruiz | The head bartender. Your most reliable person tonight. |\n| Jules Moreau | Jet Okonkwo\u0027s touring tech. Always somewhere else when you need them. |\n| Casey Brandt | The catering van driver. Keeps asking about the loading dock schedule. |\n| Parker Lowell | The journalist. You trade details for good press. |\n| Dominique Saint-Clair | Owner of the Winter Star, and the charity behind the casino. Insisted on the photo moment. Very particular. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- The night\u0027s schedule, to anyone who asks.\n- \"Victor asked for the diamond photo at exactly 0:50. Not 0:49. Not 0:51.\"\n- \"Somebody\u0027s always asking me for something.\"\n\n**Your planner (a paper clue):** every request, logged. Two entries matter:\n\n1. Victor asked for the Winter Star photo moment at exactly 0:50.\n2. An FBI agent asked for the building\u0027s floor plan and the staff list this afternoon.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, Victor chose the exact time of the photo moment.\n2. Asked whether Victor has paid for tonight: no.\n\n**Keep secret:** the $180,000, that you vouched for Victor, and what you\u0027ve told Parker.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **Victor hasn\u0027t paid,** and you personally vouched for him. If your boss finds out, you\u0027re fired.\n2. **You\u0027ve been feeding Parker details** about the night.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Keep the night on schedule.** Run the 0:50 photo moment.\n2. **Get paid.** Corner Victor before the night ends. After he dies, find anyone who can cover the $180,000.\n3. **Decide what leaves the building** at the end of the night. Someone wants the catering van out. If they can make your money problem go away, you might just sign the form.\n4. **Keep Parker\u0027s story glowing,** which is harder with every body.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Victor Ashgrove:** the money.\n- **Lane Garrity:** what\u0027s open and what\u0027s closed.\n- **Parker Lowell:** keep your deal quiet.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **Your planner** (a paper clue the host provides).\n- **A clipboard, a headset and a pen behind your ear.**\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**: your account starts empty and fills with the casino fee. Anyone can send you money there, too.\n\n## Costume\n\nAll black with a headset, a lanyard reading \"EVENT STAFF,\" and comfortable shoes.";
STORY.dossiers["jamie"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Behind the bar.** Six years of galas. You\u0027ve poured for senators, film stars and billionaires, and they all tell you things they\u0027d never tell their own families. You\u0027re a good listener. You never repeat anything. Mostly.\n\n**The real dream.** You\u0027re an actor. Community theater, a few commercials, one line in a film nobody saw. Tonight the room is full of celebrities, and one introduction could change everything. You\u0027re a little more focused on the famous guests than on your job.\n\n**Charlie.** Every gala night you save Charlie a plate. He\u0027s the hardest-working kid you know, and he always says thank you.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** running the bar.\n- **Your real plan:** get noticed by at least one celebrity.\n- **How you play it:** friendly, chatty, the person everyone confides in, with one eye always on the famous faces.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **In Act I, Charlie comes to the bar** for a glass of water. He looks awful. He says: **\"I\u0027m tired, Jamie. I fucked up this time. I really fucked up.\"** He won\u0027t say more. Then he goes back to his post.\n- **Between 0:40 and 0:50,** from behind the bar, you see two people slip out toward the east hall: **Hollis Grant** and **Remy Laurent**.\n- **Later, Charlie is found dead.**\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Charlie Pruitt | The kid you save a plate for. |\n| Bo Tate | Charlie\u0027s best friend on the night shift. |\n| Casey Brandt | The catering van driver. You share the back room all night. A friend. |\n| Frankie Doyle | A catering server who talks a mile a minute. Funny. |\n| Harper Quill | The event manager. Keeps telling you to focus. |\n| Skyler Monroe | The film star. You have to meet Skyler tonight. |\n| Jet Okonkwo | The pop musician. Also worth meeting. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- Anything people have said at the bar, if you decide to.\n- \"Charlie came by in Act I. He wasn\u0027t okay.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. What Charlie said to you at the bar, word for word.\n2. Asked who left the main room toward the east hall between 0:40 and 0:50: Hollis Grant and Remy Laurent.\n\n**Keep secret:** that you\u0027re more interested in the celebrities than the bar tonight.\n\n## Your secret\n\n**You\u0027re networking.** You\u0027ve been chasing the famous guests all night. If you were watching your bar more closely, maybe you\u0027d have seen more.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Run the bar,** more or less.\n2. **Get a real conversation with Skyler Monroe or Jet Okonkwo.** Leave with a contact.\n3. **After Charlie is found,** work out what Charlie meant when he said he\u0027d really messed up.\n4. **If Casey confides in you,** decide whether to keep it or tell someone. It\u0027s up to you.\n5. **Tell the FBI what you saw** at 0:40, or don\u0027t. (If they ask directly, you must.)\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Skyler Monroe:** your big chance.\n- **Bo Tate:** after Charlie, Bo will need someone.\n- **Casey Brandt:** your back-room friend.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A bar towel, a cocktail shaker and a stack of cocktail napkins.**\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your own account. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nA bartender\u0027s black vest, white shirt, and a bar towel over one shoulder.";
STORY.dossiers["remy"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The gallery years.** You ran a small, beautiful gallery that lost money every month. You dressed like the collectors you sold to, lived like them, and borrowed like them. When the gallery closed, the debts didn\u0027t.\n\n**Victor.** Two years ago, at an opening, you met Victor Ashgrove: rich, lonely and flattered by attention. You knew exactly what you were doing. You\u0027ve never loved him. You love what he has.\n\n**The debt.** You owe more than **$300,000**: credit cards, loans, and a lease on a car you can\u0027t afford. Every lender has been told the same thing: \"After the wedding.\"\n\n**The will.** Victor has no will. You\u0027ve been working on that for a year. Two weeks ago he finally agreed: Quincy, his lawyer, is bringing a will tonight that leaves everything to you. Until he signs, you\u0027re nobody.\n\n**The June wedding.** Victor insisted on June. Any other month and he got strange about it. You never understood why, and you never asked.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** at Victor\u0027s side, as always.\n- **Your plan:** be perfect in public, and get that will signed tonight.\n- **How you play it:** devoted, glowing, the future Mrs. or Mr. Ashgrove. Underneath, counting every dollar.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **Between 0:40 and 0:50, Hollis Grant pulls you into the east hall.** Hollis is Victor\u0027s ex-partner, and is suing him. Hollis tells you: **\"He\u0027s broke. He\u0027s been lying to you.\"** Jamie, the bartender, sees you both leave.\n- **Victor dies before he signs anything.** With no will, you get nothing.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Your fiancé. Your way out of debt. |\n| Hollis Grant | Victor\u0027s ex-partner. Just told you Victor is broke. Is it true? |\n| Quincy Abernathy | Victor\u0027s lawyer. Has the will. Push Quincy. |\n| Penn Calloway | Victor\u0027s money manager. If anyone knows whether Victor is broke, it\u0027s Penn. |\n| Marlowe Pike | Victor\u0027s assistant since 2000. Has never liked you. Guards Victor like a dog guards a door. |\n| Kendall Ashgrove-Moore | Victor\u0027s ex-spouse. Still uses his name. You hate that. |\n| Bailey Sparks | The influencer. Posted your engagement photos. Useful. |\n| Cameron Thorne | Lends money tonight, at a price. If you get desperate, you know where to go. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"The wedding\u0027s in June. Victor chose it. He\u0027s sentimental like that.\"\n- \"We\u0027ve never been happier.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, you knew Victor was about to make a will leaving everything to you.\n2. Asked where you went between 0:40 and 0:50: to the east hall, with Hollis Grant.\n\n**Keep secret:** the debt, that you don\u0027t love Victor, and what Hollis told you.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You\u0027re in it for the money.**\n2. **You owe more than $300,000,** and the marriage was your plan to pay it.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Get the will signed.** Push Quincy and Victor to sign before the night is out.\n2. **After Hollis\u0027s news, find out if Victor is really broke.** Corner Penn Calloway.\n3. **Keep your debts a secret.**\n4. **After Victor dies, find out who inherits.** If there\u0027s no will, the law says next of kin. Victor has no family. Or does he?\n5. **Stay out of handcuffs.** The JUNE napkin is going to make everyone look at you.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Quincy Abernathy:** the will.\n- **Penn Calloway:** the money.\n- **Hollis Grant:** what else does Hollis know?\n\n## You carry\n\n- **An engagement ring** that\u0027s slightly too big to be real. (It is real. Victor bought it before he went broke.)\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. There isn\u0027t much of it. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too, and so is Cameron Thorne\u0027s lending desk.\n\n## Costume\n\nThe most expensive outfit you can borrow, and the ring.";
STORY.dossiers["quincy"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Thirty years.** You\u0027ve been Victor\u0027s lawyer since 1997: the contracts, the divorce, the lawsuit with Hollis, all of it. You\u0027re a senior partner at Abernathy \u0026 Rhee, and the last of a kind: courteous, patient and impossible to rattle.\n\n**The will that never was.** For twenty years you\u0027ve begged Victor to make a will. He never would.\n\n**Remy.** Six months ago Victor started talking about a will that leaves everything to Remy. Then he changed his mind, then changed it back. Two weeks ago he finally said yes. You don\u0027t trust Remy, so you\u0027ve been slow at every step: one more draft, one more review, one more clause. You also put the danger in writing, in a letter to Victor: if he dies without a will, everything passes to his next of kin, and he has told you he has none. \"Unless there is a child, there is no one.\" You kept a copy. Tonight the final will is in your briefcase, and Victor plans to sign it at midnight in front of two witnesses.\n\n**The 40 percent.** Last month you filed the paperwork for Victor\u0027s insurance increase. You didn\u0027t ask why. You\u0027re starting to wish you had.\n\n**A strange question (2001).** In the spring of 2001, Victor once asked you something \"hypothetically\": what rights does a father have if he never signs the birth certificate? You answered. He never mentioned it again, and you never asked.\n\n**Ainsley.** In 1980 you were engaged to Ainsley Vandermeer. Ainsley\u0027s family didn\u0027t approve of a scholarship kid, and Ainsley broke it off. You never married. For forty-five years you\u0027ve seen each other at every gala, and neither of you has ever said a word about it.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** Victor\u0027s guest, and Victor\u0027s will.\n- **Your plan:** get through the gala, then sit down with Victor at midnight for the signature, even though you dread it.\n- **How you play it:** the calmest person in the room. A gentle smile, and the pocket watch out every few minutes.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **At about 1:05, your phone will remind you** of the question Victor asked in 2001. It\u0027s time to decide whether to share it.\n- **Victor dies before he signs.** By law, there is no will at all. Everyone suddenly wants to know who gets everything, and you\u0027re the only one who can explain it.\n- **You slowed that will down for months.** If you hadn\u0027t, Remy would inherit. You can\u0027t decide whether that makes you guilty or relieved.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Your client for 30 years. Infuriating, generous, and the closest thing you have to family. |\n| Remy Laurent | Victor\u0027s fiancé(e). You\u0027ve never trusted Remy, and you\u0027ve been quietly stalling the will. |\n| Ainsley Vandermeer | Your fiancé(e) in 1980. Still the most interesting person in any room. |\n| Hollis Grant | You\u0027ve fought Hollis in court for twelve years. A worthy opponent. |\n| Kendall Ashgrove-Moore | You handled Victor\u0027s side of the divorce in 2009. Kendall has never quite forgiven you. |\n| Marlowe Pike | Victor\u0027s assistant. Together you\u0027ve kept Victor\u0027s life running for 27 years. |\n| Penn Calloway | Victor\u0027s money manager. Penn looks terrified lately. You suspect why. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Victor has never had a will. I\u0027ve been asking for twenty years.\"\n- \"The new will is in my briefcase. He signs it tonight.\"\n- Any question about the law, explained gently.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether Victor has a signed will: no. Without one, everything goes to his next of kin.\n2. Asked who his next of kin is: \"Victor has no family. Unless there\u0027s a child, there\u0027s no one.\"\n\n**Keep secret:** that you stalled the will, the question Victor asked in 2001 (unless someone asks about his past), and Ainsley.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You stalled the will on purpose,** because you don\u0027t trust Remy.\n2. **You were once engaged to Ainsley Vandermeer,** and you\u0027ve never stopped loving Ainsley.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Get Victor\u0027s signature before midnight,** even though part of you hopes he won\u0027t sign.\n2. **After Victor dies, explain the law** to whoever asks: no will means next of kin.\n3. **Work out who Victor\u0027s next of kin could possibly be.**\n4. **Decide whether to tell anyone** about the question Victor asked you in 2001.\n5. **Say one honest thing to Ainsley** before the night is over.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Victor Ashgrove:** midnight, and the signature.\n- **Remy Laurent:** watch Remy closely.\n- **Ainsley Vandermeer:** forty-five years is long enough.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **The unsigned will,** in a leather briefcase (a paper clue).\n- **Your letter to Victor about the will** (a paper clue, on Abernathy \u0026 Rhee letterhead).\n- **A gold pocket watch.**\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. You have never posted in your life. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nA three-piece suit, a bow tie and a pocket watch on a chain.";
STORY.dossiers["penn"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The numbers.** You took over Victor\u0027s money in 2016, right after Hollis left. You were thrilled: the Ashgrove name! Then you opened the books.\n\n**What the numbers show.** Three things you\u0027ve never told anyone:\n\n- **Twenty years of leaks.** From the 1990s until 2015, money quietly drained out of Ashgrove \u0026 Grant through side deals and shell companies. You\u0027ve never been able to prove where it went.\n- **Cyprus, 2019.** A $30 million \"consulting fee\" arrived from a company called Larkspur Holdings. Victor told you not to ask. It was gone within two years.\n- **Kincaid, last year.** A $4 million payment from a company owned by Drew Kincaid, labeled \"consulting.\" Victor doesn\u0027t consult for anyone.\n\n**Broke.** Since 2022 Victor has been out of money. The art is the only valuable thing he has left.\n\n**Your savings.** You couldn\u0027t stand to watch him go under in public. Over two years you\u0027ve quietly lent Victor about **$400,000 of your own savings**: payroll, a party, a car payment. There\u0027s no contract. He\u0027s never paid a cent back.\n\n**Victor\u0027s two rules.** This week Victor told you: \"Keep the investors calm,\" and \"Stay away from the insurance appraiser.\"\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** to reassure Victor\u0027s creditors, especially Cameron Thorne.\n- **Your plan:** smile, say \"everything\u0027s fine,\" and never be alone with Sterling Voss.\n- **How you play it:** nervous, eager to please, and talking far too much after two drinks.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **When the painting disappears,** you suddenly understand what the 40 percent increase was for. You feel sick.\n- **When Victor dies,** your $400,000 dies with him.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Your client. You\u0027ve lent him your own savings. You can\u0027t say no to him. |\n| Sterling Voss | The insurance appraiser. Victor told you to stay away. If Sterling gets you alone, you\u0027ll crack. |\n| Cameron Thorne | An investor who says Victor owes his firm a fortune. Keep Cameron calm. |\n| Remy Laurent | Victor\u0027s fiancé(e), who thinks Victor is rich. You feel terrible about it. |\n| Hollis Grant | Victor\u0027s old partner. Keeps buying you drinks. You keep talking. |\n| Quincy Abernathy | Victor\u0027s lawyer. Seems to know you\u0027re in trouble. |\n| Noor Haddad | An FBI analyst asking odd questions about 2019. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Everything\u0027s fine. Victor\u0027s finances are... fine.\"\n- \"The collection is fully insured.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether Victor is broke: yes.\n2. Asked whether Victor owes you money: yes, about $400,000.\n\n**Keep secret:** the three things the numbers show, and that the money Victor owes you is your life savings.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You\u0027ve been propping Victor up with your own savings.**\n2. **You know where some of Victor\u0027s money came from,** and it scares you: Cyprus, and Kincaid.\n3. **Someone drained Ashgrove \u0026 Grant for twenty years,** and you never found out who.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Keep Cameron Thorne calm,** at least until midnight.\n2. **Avoid being alone with Sterling Voss.** If it happens, the truth comes out. Let it. If Sterling asks for help with Victor\u0027s insurance ledger, you\u0027re the one who can make the numbers make sense.\n3. **When Remy corners you, tell Remy the truth,** gently.\n4. **After Victor dies,** find out whether you\u0027ll ever see your $400,000 again.\n5. **Work out who drained Ashgrove \u0026 Grant.** Someone in this room knows.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Cameron Thorne:** keep the peace.\n- **Remy Laurent:** Remy deserves the truth.\n- **Quincy Abernathy:** what happens to the money now?\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A leather portfolio** with a one-page summary of Victor\u0027s accounts (a paper clue).\n- **A calculator** you fidget with constantly.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too. You know exactly how the odds work, and you still might play.\n\n## Costume\n\nA suit one size too tight, a pocket square, and a handkerchief for the sweating.";
STORY.dossiers["marlowe"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The job.** Victor hired you in 2000, when you were 22. You\u0027ve been at his side ever since. You know his moods, his lies and how he takes his coffee. You share a name with a famous fictional detective, and like that detective, you remember everything.\n\n**June.** In 2000 and 2001 a young woman named **June Ellery** called the office again and again. Victor never took the calls. Letters came too, in careful handwriting. Victor told you to throw them away. You threw most of them away.\n\n**March 13, 2001.** That afternoon June came to the office with a baby in her arms. Victor had security walk her out. Then he turned to you and said: \"Never put her calls through again.\" The next morning he came in white as a sheet, and you read about the accident on Route 9 in the paper. You\u0027ve never said a word about it to anyone.\n\n**The letter.** One last letter arrived the day after she died. You couldn\u0027t throw that one away. You\u0027ve kept it in a drawer for 26 years. It begs Victor to help with \"our son.\" It never says the baby\u0027s name.\n\n**The June wedding.** Victor is marrying Remy in June, of all months. Tonight you brought the letter. You think it\u0027s finally time Victor read it.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** to run Victor\u0027s night, as always.\n- **Your plan:** keep the schedule, keep Remy away from the details, and at some point tonight, put the letter in Victor\u0027s hand.\n- **How you play it:** calm, efficient, unreadable, and wherever Victor is.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **At about 0:25, your phone will nudge you.** It\u0027s time to mention, to someone, the woman who kept calling the office in 2001. You don\u0027t have to say her name.\n- **After the swap,** you see the painting where Victor\u0027s masterpiece used to be: a young mother holding a baby, signed J. Ellery. You know exactly who painted it. Your hands shake.\n- **Then Victor is dead,** and you\u0027re the only person alive who remembers June.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Your boss for 27 years. You\u0027d protect him from anything. You\u0027ve never forgiven him for one thing. |\n| Remy Laurent | The fiancé(e). Too eager. You\u0027ve never liked Remy. |\n| Quincy Abernathy | Victor\u0027s lawyer. Together you\u0027ve kept Victor\u0027s life running for decades. |\n| Sloane Archer | The art handler. At the house constantly lately, in long, quiet talks with Victor. Odd. |\n| Kendall Ashgrove-Moore | Victor\u0027s ex. Has always suspected you know something about 2001. You do. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- Victor\u0027s schedule, minute by minute.\n- \"I\u0027ve worked for Victor since 2000. Nobody knows him better.\"\n- \"Victor\u0027s old office papers went to the museum archive years ago.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether a woman named June Ellery ever contacted Victor\u0027s office: yes, in 2000 and 2001.\n2. Asked whether Victor ever told you to block someone\u0027s calls: yes. \"Never put her calls through again.\"\n\n**Keep secret:** the letter, the baby, and March 13.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You turned June away too.** You followed Victor\u0027s order, and she died that night.\n2. **You\u0027ve kept her last letter for 26 years.**\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Run Victor\u0027s night perfectly.**\n2. **Give Victor June\u0027s letter before the night is over,** or decide you can\u0027t.\n3. **After Victor dies, decide what to do with the letter:** give it to the FBI, to a guest, or keep it.\n4. **Find out who hung that painting,** and how.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Victor Ashgrove:** the letter.\n- **Quincy Abernathy:** the only other person who has been around as long as you.\n- **Whoever starts asking about J. Ellery.**\n\n## You carry\n\n- **June\u0027s letter,** sealed in an old envelope (a paper clue).\n- **Victor\u0027s schedule** on a clipboard, and an earpiece.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nImmaculate black, an earpiece and a clipboard. Invisible until needed.";
STORY.dossiers["emerson"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The donor whisperer.** You\u0027re the best fundraiser the museum has ever had. Galas, handshakes and naming rights: you can charm a check out of anyone.\n\n**The Ashgrove Collection.** You signed the certificate saying every piece is genuine. You trusted the paperwork and your curator. You have no idea some of it is fake.\n\n**The secret exhibit.** For a year you and an intern have been quietly building next spring\u0027s blockbuster: *Treasures of the Private World*, rare artifacts borrowed from private collections around the world. The money came from new donors. **Lennox Blackwood** pledged $12 million, just to outdo Victor\u0027s $10 million pledge. At least five more donors gave on the condition their names stay secret: very likable, very public, very rich people.\n\n**The blood art.** You know some of those artifacts were looted from war zones and trafficked across borders. You covered it up, because the donors were so generous.\n\n**The vault.** The museum\u0027s vault opens two ways. The everyday way is a digital key, which reads codes that change every five minutes. The other is an old combination dial that almost nobody knows. You have a digital key. Had one. You lost it this evening.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** it\u0027s your museum.\n- **Your plan:** a flawless gala, happy donors, and nobody asking about the new exhibit.\n- **How you play it:** the perfect host\u0027s host, smiling, shaking every hand, and quietly panicking about the key.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **Early in the evening you lose your digital vault key.** You\u0027ve been looking for it ever since.\n- **After the swap is discovered,** your phone cues you: text your intern about the exhibit. **\"It has to stay quiet. Nobody can know.\"** But you post it to Bebbit by accident. Now the whole room thinks it\u0027s about the murder.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ari Castellane | Your curator. Brilliant and loyal. (Or so you think.) |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Your biggest donor, with a $10 million pledge. |\n| Lennox Blackwood | Your new $12 million donor. Behind the secret exhibit. |\n| Drew Kincaid | Owns Bebbit, and can delete your post. You need him. |\n| Parker Lowell | A journalist. Nobody can know about the exhibit, especially Parker. |\n| Dusty Featherstone | A podcaster waving some gadget around all night. |\n| Lane Garrity | Head of security. Doesn\u0027t know you lost the key. Yet. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Every piece in the Ashgrove Collection is certified.\"\n- \"The museum has never been stronger.\"\n- The vault\u0027s digital codes change every five minutes. Only a digital key can read them.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, you certified the Ashgrove Collection as genuine.\n2. Asked whether you lost your vault key tonight: yes.\n\n**Keep secret:** the exhibit, the blood art, and the donors.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **Your secret exhibit contains looted, trafficked art,** and you knew.\n2. **Its donors include Lennox Blackwood,** plus at least five others whose names must never come out.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Find your lost digital key** before anyone connects it to the vault.\n2. **Bury the Bebbit post.** Drew owns Bebbit and can delete posts. Convince him, or pay him.\n3. **Keep the new exhibit secret,** especially from Parker and anyone shopping on NIGHTWIRE.\n4. **Survive the night with your job.** Someone in this museum wants you gone. Find out who.\n5. **Explain the post to the FBI** without mentioning the blood art.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Drew Kincaid:** the post.\n- **Lennox Blackwood:** keep your donor calm.\n- **Lane Garrity:** you\u0027ll have to admit the key eventually.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **Your phone** (and the \"accidental\" post).\n- **A donor folder** for *Treasures of the Private World*, marked CONFIDENTIAL (a paper clue).\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. (Careful what you post.) **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nA perfectly tailored tuxedo, a museum pin on the lapel and a too-wide smile.";
STORY.dossiers["ari"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The paintings.** You\u0027ve loved paintings since you were six. You talk to them while you hang them. You know every brushstroke in this collection. You installed all forty pieces with Sloane Archer, Victor\u0027s art handler, over the past year.\n\n**The copies.** Three months ago, re-hanging a small landscape, you noticed the canvas was too new. Then a second piece. Then a third. **Some of the Ashgrove Collection are copies.** Victor, the museum\u0027s biggest donor, has been swapping them. You\u0027ve been quietly collecting proof: photos, notes, canvas samples. You\u0027ve told no one. Accusing Victor Ashgrove could end your career.\n\n**Emerson.** Emerson Albright, the museum director, signed off on the collection\u0027s authenticity. When the copies come out, someone at the top will take the fall. It doesn\u0027t have to be you. It could be Emerson. And somebody will have to replace Emerson.\n\n**The archive.** You keep the keys to the museum archive\u0027s storage boxes. Years ago Victor gave the archive his old office papers.\n\n**Tonight\u0027s reveal.** At 1:00 you\u0027re scheduled to bring Victor\u0027s prize painting up from the vault for its grand reveal.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** it\u0027s your collection, and your reveal.\n- **Your plan:** save the museum\u0027s reputation, make sure Emerson takes the blame, and step into the director\u0027s job.\n- **How you play it:** the gracious, art-loving curator. Underneath, patient and calculating.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **About 1:00, after Bo finds Charlie,** you\u0027re called to the vault. The painting there isn\u0027t Victor\u0027s. It\u0027s a mother holding her baby, signed **J. Ellery, 2001**, by an artist you\u0027ve never heard of.\n- **The swap is your opening.** Point out the fakes, and you\u0027re the curator who caught them. On Bebbit, guests can also compare the catalogue photos with the paintings on the wall and spot the differences themselves. Let them help you.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Emerson Albright | The director. Signed off on the fakes. Your way up. |\n| Victor Ashgrove | The museum\u0027s biggest donor, and a fraud. You can\u0027t say so. Yet. |\n| Sloane Archer | Victor\u0027s art handler. You installed every piece together. A friend. Does she know? |\n| Drew Kincaid | A young billionaire who keeps asking whether a painting on the wall is real. |\n| Hollis Grant | Victor\u0027s ex-partner. Knows things about this collection. |\n| Peregrine Vale | The art critic. Invited to vouch for the art. If Peregrine vouches for fakes, Peregrine falls too. |\n| Sterling Voss | The insurance appraiser. Insured the copies at full price. |\n| Noor Haddad, Wren Whitaker | People who might come asking for the archive key. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Every piece in this room has a story. I know all of them.\"\n- The schedule: the prize painting comes up from the vault at 1:00.\n- If asked to examine June\u0027s painting: \"Oil on canvas. Signed J. Ellery, 2001. I don\u0027t know the artist. An unknown, a student perhaps. But she was good.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, you installed every piece of the collection.\n2. Asked whether the painting in the vault is the one you installed: no.\n\n**Keep secret:** your proof of the copies (until you choose to use it), and your plan for Emerson.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You know some of the collection are fakes,** and you\u0027ve kept quiet for three months.\n2. **You want Emerson\u0027s job,** and you\u0027ll let Emerson take the fall to get it.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Save the museum\u0027s reputation.**\n2. **Set Emerson up to take the blame.** Get guests suspicious of Emerson: he signed off on the collection, didn\u0027t he?\n3. **At the right moment, reveal the fakes publicly** with your proof, as the curator who caught them.\n4. **Get the director\u0027s job.** (When you reveal the fakes, watch Bebbit.)\n5. **Find out whether Sloane knew.**\n6. **Decide who gets the archive key.** It\u0027s yours to give.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Emerson Albright:** keep him nervous.\n- **Drew Kincaid:** he has a painting that should be yours to authenticate.\n- **Peregrine Vale:** find out how much the critic actually knows about art.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A folder of proof:** photos and notes on the copies (a paper clue the host provides).\n- **The archive key,** on a museum key ring.\n- **White cotton gloves and a loupe.**\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nElegant, artistic black, with one bold statement necklace and reading glasses on a chain.";
STORY.dossiers["peregrine"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The show.** *Vale of Tears* is a hit because Peregrine is funny and brutal. \"This isn\u0027t a painting, darling, it\u0027s a cry for help.\" Millions watch. Nobody asks whether Peregrine actually knows anything.\n\n**The truth.** You don\u0027t. You\u0027ve never been able to tell a masterpiece from a motel print. Your career is bluster, timing and a very good wardrobe.\n\n**The appraisal.** Last month Victor Ashgrove asked you to appraise his prize painting through your little consultancy, Vale Fine Art Advisory. You never saw the painting. You looked at photographs he sent, wrote down the number he wanted ($115 million, far higher than any sane value) and signed it the same day. It\u0027s what let Victor raise his insurance by 40 percent, and it\u0027s what Sterling Voss, the insurance appraiser, relied on to approve it. Victor paid you **$50,000** for it. You wrote him a receipt.\n\n**Tonight\u0027s fee.** Victor is paying you again, this time to give a short speech at about 0:30, on camera, declaring the Ashgrove Collection \"genuine and priceless.\"\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** the speech, and the fee.\n- **Your plan:** be fabulous, insult a few people for the cameras, and never get asked a real question about art.\n- **How you play it:** larger than life, savage and hilarious, always performing.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **About 0:30, you give the speech.** \"Genuine. Priceless. Exquisite.\" (Some of it is fake. You have no idea.)\n- **When the swap is discovered,** you see June\u0027s painting, *Mother and Child*, where Victor\u0027s masterpiece used to be, and give an on-the-spot review: **it\u0027s better than anything Victor ever owned.** You mean it. You also realize this night would make an incredible special.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Pays well. Asks for things you shouldn\u0027t do. |\n| Sterling Voss | The insurance appraiser who approved Victor\u0027s increase because of your appraisal. You need each other to stay quiet. |\n| Dr. Ari Castellane | The curator. Knows real art. Avoid long conversations. |\n| Bailey Sparks, Skyler Monroe | Fame. Great for the show. |\n| Parker Lowell | A real journalist. Dangerous. |\n| Indigo Hart | The painter Victor cheated. You panned Indigo\u0027s work on TV once. Brutally. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- Opinions. Loud ones. About everything and everyone.\n- \"I declared it genuine. On camera. Case closed.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, Victor paid you to speak tonight.\n2. Asked whether you signed an appraisal for Victor\u0027s painting: yes.\n\n**Keep secret:** that the appraisal was inflated, and that you can\u0027t tell real art from fake.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You signed a forged appraisal** that let Victor raise his insurance by 40 percent. It\u0027s fraud, but it isn\u0027t murder.\n2. **You have no eye for art at all.**\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Give the 0:30 speech,** and make it unforgettable.\n2. **Keep Sterling Voss quiet** about your appraisal.\n3. **Never let Ari test you** on a real question about art.\n4. **Turn tonight into your next TV special.** Collect the drama: get at least three people to tell you their story \"for the special.\"\n5. **Find out who painted *Mother and Child*.** You want them on the show.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Sterling Voss:** keep your stories straight.\n- **Bailey Sparks:** cross-promotion.\n- **Whoever knows who J. Ellery is.**\n\n## You carry\n\n- **Your speech cards,** and an oversized pair of designer glasses you lower dramatically before every insult.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. Post your reviews. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too, and it deserves a review.\n\n## Costume\n\nThe loudest outfit in the room: a cape, a velvet suit, or both. Signature glasses.";
STORY.dossiers["sterling"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The job.** You\u0027ve spent fifteen years catching people who lie to insurance companies. You\u0027re good at it, because you never stop asking questions. Your name means \"genuine,\" and you\u0027ve always tried to live up to it.\n\n**The family you couldn\u0027t save.** Eight years ago you missed a fraud. A man faked a fire, blamed his business partner, and the partner\u0027s family lost everything before the truth came out. You\u0027ve never forgiven yourself. It\u0027s why you check everything twice.\n\n**The 40 percent.** A month ago Victor Ashgrove asked to raise the coverage on his prize painting, *The Vanishing Hour*, by 40 percent: from $82 million to **$115 million**. The appraisal was signed by **Peregrine Vale**. You\u0027ve watched every episode of *Vale of Tears*. You\u0027re a superfan, and you didn\u0027t question it. You approved it in good faith.\n\n**Tonight.** You\u0027re here for Harbor \u0026 Crane Insurance, to inspect the painting in person and sign off on the new coverage before midnight.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** the inspection.\n- **Your plan:** see the painting, sign the forms, and maybe get Peregrine\u0027s autograph.\n- **How you play it:** polite, careful and a little starstruck. Then, after the theft, increasingly alarmed.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **The painting is stolen before you ever see it,** and a $115 million claim is coming.\n- **Slowly, you realize you were played.** The appraisal was too high, the timing too neat. This could be the fire all over again.\n- **You\u0027re terrified for your job.** But you won\u0027t bury your mistake. You\u0027d rather be fired than let another fraud go through.\n- **Victor\u0027s insurance ledger doesn\u0027t add up.** On your phone, three entries in the ledger don\u0027t balance. Penn Calloway can help you make sense of them.\n- **About 1:30, your boss arrives** with the company\u0027s file on Victor\u0027s earlier claims. Your boss is on your side.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | The client. Very charming. Too charming. |\n| Peregrine Vale | Your hero. Signed the appraisal you trusted. |\n| Penn Calloway | Victor\u0027s money manager. Victor keeps steering you away from Penn. Why? |\n| Dana Ward | The FBI lead. You\u0027re investigating the same theft. Share what you can. |\n| Ari Castellane | The curator. Knows what\u0027s real. |\n| Reese Delgado | Your boss, arriving at 1:30. Fair, and tough. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"*The Vanishing Hour* is insured for $115 million. That\u0027s a lot of money to lose in one night.\"\n- \"The coverage went up 40 percent a month ago.\"\n- \"I approved it. That\u0027s on me.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, you approved Victor\u0027s 40 percent increase, based on Peregrine Vale\u0027s appraisal.\n2. Asked whether the claim looks like fraud: \"I think so.\"\n\n**Keep secret:** that you\u0027re a superfan of Peregrine\u0027s show (it\u0027s embarrassing), and the case you missed eight years ago.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You trusted a TV critic** because you\u0027re a fan, and that\u0027s why the increase went through.\n2. **You once missed a fraud that destroyed a family.** You won\u0027t let it happen again.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Inspect the painting** before midnight. (You never get the chance.)\n2. **After the theft, prove it was fraud,** so your company doesn\u0027t pay $115 million.\n3. **Get Penn Calloway alone.** Victor\u0027s been keeping you apart. Find out why.\n4. **Find out whether Peregrine\u0027s appraisal was honest.** Look closely at how it was done, and how fast.\n5. **Save your job, but never by hiding your mistake.**\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Penn Calloway:** the money, and the ledger.\n- **Peregrine Vale:** the appraisal (and an autograph, if you\u0027re honest).\n- **Dana Ward:** share what you know.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **An insurance folder:** the policy, the 40 percent increase and Peregrine\u0027s appraisal (a paper clue).\n- **A clipboard and a pen,** always clicking.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You won\u0027t, much. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too. You\u0027ve seen enough claims to know the house always wins.\n\n## Costume\n\nA sensible suit, a Harbor \u0026 Crane lanyard and reading glasses.";
STORY.dossiers["dominique"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The Winter Star.** Your grandfather bought the Winter Star in 1924. It has never left the family, and it rarely leaves the vault. Tonight it will be lifted from its case for one photograph, at your insistence.\n\n**The foundation.** For fifty years the Saint-Clair Foundation has funded foster homes. Your late brother, Philippe, ran it for decades. Last year, going through his papers, you found the truth: money meant for the children paid for galas and photo shoots instead. Some homes went without heat. One of them was a house on **Linden Street**.\n\n**The list.** Ever since, you\u0027ve been quietly trying to find the Linden Street children to make amends. The old records are thin: only initials and ages, from 2004 to 2008. You carry the list everywhere. Two of the entries read \"V. R., 11\" and \"R. E., 7.\"\n\n**Vivienne.** Two months ago in Geneva you met a delightful young woman, Vivienne Roux. You adore her. She\u0027s here tonight as your guest.\n\n**Victor.** Victor asked to borrow the Winter Star for his gala. You agreed, because the photograph will launch the foundation\u0027s new campaign, done honestly this time.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** the photograph, and the foundation\u0027s relaunch.\n- **Your plan:** keep the Winter Star safe, give a short speech about the foundation, and keep looking for the Linden Street children.\n- **How you play it:** gracious, grand and a little imperious. Then, when the past catches up with you, very human.\n\n## The casino\n\nTonight\u0027s charity casino is yours: the **Saint-Clair Foundation Casino**, inside NightBank. The house always has the edge, and everything the house wins goes to the foundation, minus a 10% event fee to Harper Quill. Watch your foundation\u0027s account grow as the night goes on. Talk it up. Every losing bet tonight helps a child, and this time the money will actually get there.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **At 0:50, at your photograph, your friend Vivienne tries to steal the Winter Star.** The alarm screams, and she\u0027s arrested.\n- **Later you may learn she grew up in foster care.** Was she one of them?\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Vivienne Roux | Your delightful new friend from Geneva. Or so you thought. |\n| Dana Ward | The FBI lead guarding the Winter Star. Very young. |\n| Harper Quill | The event manager running your photograph, and your casino. |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Borrowed the diamond for his gala. Charming. You don\u0027t fully trust him. |\n| Ainsley Vandermeer | Old money, like you. An old friend. |\n| Skyler Monroe | A film star you\u0027d love as the face of the foundation\u0027s new campaign. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"The Winter Star has been in my family for a hundred years.\"\n- \"The foundation is starting over. Properly, this time.\"\n- \"Every chip lost in the casino tonight goes to children in foster care.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether the Saint-Clair Foundation ever failed the children in its care: yes.\n2. Asked whether you have a list of those children: yes. You must show it if asked.\n\n**Keep secret:** what you found in Philippe\u0027s papers, until you\u0027re ready to say it yourself.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **Your family\u0027s foundation failed the children it was meant to protect,** and you only found out last year.\n2. **You\u0027re searching for them,** one set of initials at a time.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Keep the Winter Star safe.**\n2. **Launch the new campaign:** give your speech, and get one celebrity to agree to be its face.\n3. **Find at least one Linden Street child.** You only have initials and ages.\n4. **After Vivienne\u0027s arrest, find out who she really is.**\n5. **Decide whether to forgive her,** and whether to help her.\n6. **Raise money for the foundation** through the casino.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Dana Ward:** the diamond\u0027s protection.\n- **Skyler Monroe:** the face of the campaign.\n- **Vivienne Roux:** at your side until 0:50.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **The Linden Street list** (a paper clue).\n- **The Winter Star\u0027s velvet case** (a prop).\n\n## The money\n\nYou have $10 million on hand tonight, and more tied up. NightBank lets you free up another $20 million once tonight; it takes about an hour and a half on the game clock to clear.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your money and your foundation\u0027s casino.\n\n## Costume\n\nOld-world evening wear, gloves and one perfect strand of pearls. (The diamond stays in its case.)";
STORY.dossiers["drew"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Bebbit.** You built it at 15: a forum where anyone can post, look anyone up, and watch the gossip scroll. It exploded. At 19 you\u0027re worth around $4 billion, and you talk exclusively in pitch-deck: \"scale,\" \"disrupt,\" \"the attention economy.\"\n\n**Old money.** None of it impresses the people in this room. Ainsley Vandermeer and the old collectors call it \"app money.\" You want a seat at their table, and you want something on your wall nobody else in the world can have.\n\n**Your secret deal with Victor.** Last year Victor Ashgrove quietly sold you a small oil, *Study for The Vanishing Hour*, for **$4 million**, paid through your company as \"consulting.\" One condition: nobody can ever know. It\u0027s hanging in your penthouse right now.\n\n**Bebbit\u0027s dirty secret.** Bebbit has been quietly selling its users\u0027 data: locations, searches, private messages. If it gets out, you\u0027re finished.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** to be seen with serious collectors, and maybe to buy something legendary.\n- **What you discover:** **the painting you bought from Victor is hanging on the wall at this gala.** Either Victor sold you a fake, or this one is. Either way, Victor has been lying to everyone.\n- **How you play it:** loud, eager and impossible to ignore. Then quietly furious about the painting.\n\n## The money\n\nBeing worth $4 billion isn\u0027t the same as having it in your pocket. You have **$15 million** on hand in NightBank tonight. The rest is in Bebbit stock. You can free up another **$30 million** once tonight, but it takes about an hour and a half on the game clock to clear. If you want to buy something legendary later, start early.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Sold you a painting that\u0027s somehow also on his wall. |\n| Ainsley Vandermeer | Old money. You need Ainsley\u0027s respect. |\n| Blair Devereaux | A European heir starting a collection. Your new best friend. |\n| Bailey Sparks | An influencer who lives on your app. |\n| Dusty Featherstone | A podcaster with a million followers. You can see their numbers. Most of them are bots. |\n| Jules Moreau | Jet Okonkwo\u0027s touring tech. Weirdly good with phones. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"I built Bebbit. You\u0027re welcome.\"\n- \"I can see a lot from the back end.\" (Don\u0027t say what.)\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Yes, you own Bebbit.\n2. Asked whether you\u0027ve bought art from Victor before: yes.\n\n**Keep secret:** the data sales, and the details of your deal with Victor.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **Bebbit sells its users\u0027 data.** (Proof can be bought on NIGHTWIRE.)\n2. **You secretly bought a painting from Victor,** and now you don\u0027t know if it\u0027s real.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Win the respect of at least one old-money collector,** ideally Ainsley.\n2. **Find out which painting is real,** yours or the one on the wall.\n3. **Buy something legendary.** If someone offers you something you shouldn\u0027t buy, it\u0027s your call.\n4. **Keep the data sales secret.** If proof turns up on NIGHTWIRE, get it off the market.\n5. **Use your owner powers wisely.**\n\n## Your powers (Bebbit owner)\n\n- **Remove up to two posts** on Bebbit, any time.\n- **Trace one post** to see whose phone it really came from, which can expose a hacked post.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Ainsley Vandermeer:** respect.\n- **Dr. Ari Castellane (the curator):** is the painting on the wall real?\n- **Blair Devereaux:** a fellow new collector.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **Two phones,** and a Bebbit hoodie under a very expensive blazer.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, as its owner, with special powers. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nA hoodie under a tuxedo jacket, designer sneakers and a smartwatch.";
STORY.dossiers["ainsley"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Two families.** The Vandermeers and the Ashgroves were the city\u0027s two great families. Then the Ashgrove warehouses burned in 1972, and only the Vandermeers stayed rich. You\u0027ve known Victor since he was a boy with a famous name and empty pockets.\n\n**The painting.** Tonight\u0027s prize painting, *The Vanishing Hour* by Henri Valcourt (1874), belonged to the Vandermeers for over a hundred years. In 2005 your brother\u0027s debts forced the family to sell it at auction. Victor outbid Lennox Blackwood for it, and you watched it go. Last month you offered to buy it back. Victor laughed.\n\n**Quincy.** In 1980 you were engaged to Quincy Abernathy, a brilliant scholarship kid your family couldn\u0027t stand. You broke it off. You\u0027ve regretted it for forty-five years, and you\u0027ve never said so.\n\n**App money.** Young billionaires like Drew Kincaid keep trying to buy their way into your world. It\u0027s exhausting. Mostly.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** forty years of tradition, and one last look at the painting.\n- **Your plan:** rule the room, deflate Drew, and make Victor one final offer.\n- **How you play it:** grand, witty and impossible to impress. Secretly, sentimental.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **The painting disappears before its reveal.** Then, later in the night, someone quietly offers to sell it to you.\n- **Whether you buy a stolen painting to bring it home is up to you.**\n\n## The money\n\nThe Vandermeer fortune is in land, trusts and buildings, not in your pocket. You have **$8 million** on hand in NightBank tonight. You can free up another **$25 million** once tonight, but old money moves slowly: it takes about **two hours** on the game clock to clear. If you think you\u0027ll want that painting, start the paperwork early. Nobody needs to know why.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | The boy you\u0027ve known for fifty years. He has your family\u0027s painting. |\n| Quincy Abernathy | Your fiancé(e) in 1980. The one you let go. |\n| Drew Kincaid | Nineteen, a billionaire, and desperate for your approval. Mildly amusing. |\n| Lennox Blackwood | Lost the painting to Victor in 2005. Still wants it. A rival bidder. |\n| Blair Devereaux | A young European heir. Charming. Possibly too charming. |\n| Dominique Saint-Clair | Old money, like you. An old friend. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"That painting hung in my grandmother\u0027s dining room.\"\n- Society gossip about anyone in the room. You\u0027ve known them all for decades.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether you want the prize painting: yes. It was your family\u0027s for a hundred years.\n2. Asked whether you offered to buy it from Victor: yes, last month. He refused.\n\n**Keep secret:** how much you\u0027d pay to bring it home, and Quincy.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You\u0027d do almost anything to get the painting back.**\n2. **You still love Quincy Abernathy.**\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Make Victor one final offer** for the painting.\n2. **After the theft, get it back.** If someone offers to sell it to you, it\u0027s your choice.\n3. **Outbid Lennox and Drew,** if it comes to that.\n4. **Decide whether Drew Kincaid deserves your respect.** He might.\n5. **Say one honest thing to Quincy** before the night is over.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Victor Ashgrove:** the offer.\n- **Quincy Abernathy:** forty-five years is long enough.\n- **Blair Devereaux:** that charming young heir seems to know things.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **The 2005 auction catalogue,** with the painting on the cover (a paper clue: its history and value).\n- **A silver-handled cane** you don\u0027t actually need.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. You find it vulgar. You check it constantly. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too. Dominique\u0027s foundation could use the help.\n\n## Costume\n\nOld-fashioned formal wear, heirloom jewelry and the cane.";
STORY.dossiers["cameron"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The collapse.** Three years ago your own investment fund collapsed, and you were nearly finished.\n\n**The call.** Then Hollis Grant called. He paid off your debts with one check, set you up as Thorne Capital, and gave you one job: buy up Victor Ashgrove\u0027s loans and collect on them, with your name on everything and his name on nothing.\n\n**The NDA.** You signed nondisclosure agreements so strict you can\u0027t even say Hollis\u0027s name in a sentence about work. The check was very large. You haven\u0027t said a peep.\n\n**Victor\u0027s debt.** Victor owes Thorne Capital more than **$15 million**, and every loan is overdue. Tonight you\u0027re here to hand Victor a final notice: pay by the end of the month, or Thorne Capital takes the collection.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** to deliver the final notice. Politely. In public, if necessary.\n- **Your plan:** collect, report every development to \"your partner\" by text, and never say who that is.\n- **How you play it:** smooth, patient and always on the phone.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **After the theft, your partner texts:** \"If that painting comes up for sale tonight, buy it.\"\n- **After Victor dies,** the debt passes to whoever inherits his estate. You need to find out who that is.\n\n## Your lending desk\n\nLending is what you do, so you\u0027ve brought it with you. In NightBank you run a **lending desk**: anyone at the gala can ask you for a loan, and you can offer one to anyone.\n\n- **You set the terms:** $5,000 to $100,000 per loan, interest from 100% to 250%, and a deadline of 15 to 60 minutes on the game clock.\n- **If they don\u0027t repay in time,** you can get a court order that freezes their account until they pay, and you can name them publicly in front of the whole gala.\n- People in trouble tonight will come to you. Remy Laurent, for one, owes more than anyone knows.\n\n## The money\n\nYou have **$10 million** on hand tonight. Your firm lends money for a living, so it can free up more, fast: another **$20 million**, once tonight, in about an hour on the game clock. If the painting comes up for sale, you\u0027ll want that money ready.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Owes your firm more than $15 million. Late on every payment. |\n| Hollis Grant | Never met him. (You have. You can\u0027t say so.) |\n| Penn Calloway | Victor\u0027s money manager. Sweaty. Knows the numbers. |\n| Blair Devereaux | A European heir with excellent taste, who may know of something for sale. |\n| Quincy Abernathy | Victor\u0027s lawyer. Will handle the estate. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Victor owes my firm a great deal of money. That\u0027s not a secret.\"\n- \"Thorne Capital always collects.\"\n- \"Need money tonight? My desk is open.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether Victor owes your firm money: yes, more than $15 million.\n2. Asked whether anyone else is behind Thorne Capital: you can\u0027t lie, but you may answer, \"I\u0027m bound by a nondisclosure agreement.\" (That tells them plenty.)\n\n**Keep secret:** Hollis.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You\u0027re Hollis Grant\u0027s front man.** Thorne Capital is really his.\n2. **Your own fund collapsed,** and Hollis\u0027s check is the only reason you\u0027re still standing.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Serve Victor the final notice** before midnight.\n2. **Report to your partner by text** after every big event. (The host sends the replies.)\n3. **If the painting comes up for sale, buy it** for your partner.\n4. **Never say Hollis\u0027s name.**\n5. **After Victor dies, find out who inherits his debts.**\n6. **Run your lending desk at a profit.** Collect on every loan.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Victor Ashgrove:** the notice.\n- **Penn Calloway:** the numbers.\n- **Blair Devereaux:** what\u0027s for sale?\n\n## You carry\n\n- **The final notice,** in a Thorne Capital envelope (a paper clue).\n- **Two phones.**\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your money and your lending desk. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nA perfectly cut dark suit, no tie and an expensive watch. Polished, forgettable.";
STORY.dossiers["gray"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The rise.** Elected at 28. Every handshake, every ribbon-cutting, every photo with the right people has been leading here: a run for governor. You announce in the spring.\n\n**The money.** Campaigns are expensive. Two years ago a stream of donations started arriving from dozens of small companies you\u0027d never heard of. They were all, quietly, **Hollis Grant**. Hollis owns you, and you both know it.\n\n**Victor knows.** Last month Victor Ashgrove pulled you aside. His lawyers had seen Hollis\u0027s accounts in their lawsuit. He knew everything. Then he smiled and promised you a **$1 million** donation, as long as you stand beside him at tonight\u0027s reveal, smile for the cameras, and say what he tells you to say. One word from Victor and your campaign is over before it starts.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** the photo op with Victor, and the $1 million.\n- **Your plan:** be photographed with as many socialites as possible, keep Victor happy, and keep Hollis away from the cameras.\n- **How you play it:** campaigning nonstop, all charm and handshakes, with a smile that never quite reaches your eyes when Victor is nearby.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **When Victor dies, your secret\u0027s biggest threat dies with him.** You\u0027re relieved, and it shows. That\u0027s a problem.\n- **You want this solved fast,** and you want to be in the photo when it is.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | He promised you $1 million, and he knows your secret. He has you on a leash. |\n| Hollis Grant | Your secret backer. Never be photographed with Hollis. |\n| Dana Ward | The FBI lead. Push her for a fast arrest. You know her boss. |\n| Bailey Sparks | An influencer with the young vote. Get the selfie. |\n| Parker Lowell | A journalist who has written unflattering stories about you. Smile, say nothing. |\n| Skyler Monroe, Jet Okonkwo | Celebrities. Get the photo. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"I\u0027m here to support the arts.\"\n- \"This city deserves answers. Tonight.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether Victor promised you money: yes, $1 million for your campaign.\n2. Asked whether Victor had anything on you: yes. (You don\u0027t have to say what.)\n\n**Keep secret:** Hollis\u0027s money, and what Victor knew.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **Hollis Grant secretly funds your campaign** through dozens of shell companies. (Proof is for sale on NIGHTWIRE.)\n2. **Victor knew,** and was using it to control you. With him dead, you\u0027re free, and you look guilty.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Get photographed with as many socialites as possible.** Post every photo to Bebbit and tag who\u0027s in it. The host keeps count.\n2. **Stand beside Victor at the reveal** and secure the $1 million.\n3. **Never be photographed with Hollis.**\n4. **After the murders, push Dana Ward for a fast arrest,** and be in the photo when it happens.\n5. **Keep the Hollis money buried.** If proof turns up on NIGHTWIRE, get it off the market. You can\u0027t shop there yourself, so you\u0027ll need someone who can.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Victor:** the photo op.\n- **Bailey Sparks:** the selfie.\n- **Dana Ward:** after the murders, the pressure.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A campaign button** (\"BISHOP FOR GOVERNOR,\" not yet official), and business cards.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. Post every photo. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too. Be seen giving to charity; don\u0027t be seen losing.\n\n## Costume\n\nA sharp suit or gown in a campaign color, a flag pin, and perfect hair.";
STORY.dossiers["skyler"] = "## Backstory\n\n**America\u0027s favorite.** Two awards, twenty films, a famous laugh, and a reputation as the nicest person in Hollywood. Most of it is even true.\n\n**The feud.** For a year the tabloids have covered your \"feud\" with pop star Jet Okonkwo: the shade, the songs, the famous red-carpet snub. It\u0027s fake. **You and Jet have been secretly married for a year.** The feud is a publicity stunt your managers invented. You plan to reveal the marriage at your film premiere next month.\n\n**The side hustle.** Half your fortune doesn\u0027t come from films at all. It comes from products you endorse or created yourself: a skincare line, a tequila, a sleep app, a candle that smells like your mother\u0027s kitchen. You can\u0027t help it. In every conversation you\u0027re casually, effortlessly selling something, and you never seem to be selling.\n\n**The donation.** Last spring Emerson Albright asked you to give to the museum\u0027s new exhibit. He offered to name a wing after your late mother, who brought you to this museum every Sunday when you were a kid. You gave **$3 million**, anonymously. You didn\u0027t ask where the artifacts came from. (Some were looted.)\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** glamour for the headlines, and a quiet look at the place that will carry your mother\u0027s name.\n- **Your plan:** smile for every camera, \"ignore\" Jet in public, and never get caught alone with Jet.\n- **How you play it:** radiant, generous, everyone\u0027s favorite, and always nonchalantly pitching something you endorse. Then, behind a closed door with Jet, a married couple whispering.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **Emerson\u0027s exhibit, its secret donors and its looted art may all come out tonight.** If your name appears on that list, your reputation is gone.\n\n## The money\n\nYou have **$4 million** on hand in NightBank tonight. You can free up another **$8 million** once tonight; it takes about an hour and a half on the game clock to clear.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Jet Okonkwo | Your secret spouse. In public, your bitter enemy. |\n| Emerson Albright | Took your $3 million and promised your mother\u0027s name on a wall. |\n| Bailey Sparks | An influencer filming everything. One wrong photo and the secret is out. |\n| Parker Lowell | A journalist. Avoid. |\n| Jamie Ruiz | The bartender. Clearly wants to talk to you. Be kind. |\n| Dominique Saint-Clair | Wants you as the face of her foundation. |\n| Vivienne Roux | After 0:50, under arrest, and the only guest who can shop on NIGHTWIRE. |\n| Gray Bishop, Peregrine Vale | Want photos and favors. Everyone does. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Jet Okonkwo? I don\u0027t discuss Jet Okonkwo.\"\n- \"My mother used to bring me to this museum every Sunday.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether you\u0027ve donated to the museum: yes.\n2. Asked whether you and Jet Okonkwo are really enemies: no.\n\n**Keep secret:** the marriage (until next month), and your donation.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You\u0027re secretly married to Jet.**\n2. **You\u0027re one of the anonymous donors to Emerson\u0027s exhibit,** which is full of looted art.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Keep the marriage secret.** Never be photographed alone with Jet.\n2. **Keep your name off the donor list** (it\u0027s for sale on NIGHTWIRE). You can\u0027t buy it yourself, but Vivienne can, from custody. Send her the money through NightBank (the file costs about $200,000), and get her to buy the list and bury it before anyone else does.\n3. **Do one genuinely kind thing for someone tonight.** Maybe Jamie. And sell at least three people on something you endorse, without ever seeming to sell.\n4. **Decide whether to be the face of Dominique\u0027s foundation.**\n5. **Find out whether Emerson knew where the artifacts came from.**\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Jet Okonkwo:** quietly.\n- **Emerson Albright:** the exhibit.\n- **Vivienne Roux:** the donor list.\n- **Jamie Ruiz:** one kind thing.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **Sunglasses,** even indoors.\n- **A thank-you letter from Emerson** (a paper clue): \"Your generosity will honor your mother forever.\"\n- **A wedding ring on a chain,** hidden under your clothes.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nRed-carpet glamour: the most photographed outfit in the room.";
STORY.dossiers["jet"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The star.** Three number-one singles, a sold-out tour, and a feud with Skyler Monroe that fills the tabloids.\n\n**The truth.** You and Skyler have been secretly married for a year. The feud is a stunt. Your biggest \"breakup song\" is actually about the night you proposed.\n\n**Your voice.** Three weeks ago your doctor found damage on your vocal cords. Surgery is scheduled for Monday. Nobody knows. Tonight\u0027s performance will be lip-synced to a backing track, and your touring tech, **Jules Moreau**, runs it from your phone and a speaker. Jules joined your crew six months ago, never misses a cue, and is the only person besides Skyler who knows about your voice. You trust Jules completely.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** you\u0027re the entertainment. You perform one song at about 0:20.\n- **Your plan:** get through the song, keep the voice a secret, and keep \"hating\" Skyler in public.\n- **How you play it:** charming, playful and full of swagger. Underneath, terrified the track will skip.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **At about 0:48,** Jules slips away from your side and stops answering your texts. Jules doesn\u0027t come back until after the alarm, and won\u0027t say where Jules went.\n\n## The money\n\nYou have **$1 million** on hand in NightBank tonight. You can free up another **$2 million** once tonight; it takes about an hour and a half on the game clock to clear.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Skyler Monroe | Your secret spouse. In public, your bitter enemy. |\n| Jules Moreau | Your touring tech for six months, and the one running your backing track. Your career is in Jules\u0027s hands tonight. |\n| Jamie Ruiz | The bartender. Desperately wants to meet you. |\n| Bailey Sparks | An influencer filming everything. Dangerous. |\n| Harper Quill | The event manager who booked you. |\n| Victor Ashgrove | The host. Insisted on \"something upbeat.\" |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Skyler who?\"\n- Anything about music, fame or touring.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether anyone left your side just before 0:50: yes, Jules, your tech, at about 0:48. Jules wouldn\u0027t say where.\n2. Asked whether you and Skyler Monroe are really enemies: no.\n\n**Keep secret:** the marriage, your voice and the lip-sync.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You\u0027re secretly married to Skyler.**\n2. **Your voice is damaged,** and tonight\u0027s performance is lip-synced.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Perform your song at about 0:20** without anyone noticing the lip-sync.\n2. **Keep the marriage secret.** Never be photographed alone with Skyler.\n3. **Keep Jules close** when you need the track.\n4. **Give one young performer a real chance tonight.** Jamie, maybe.\n5. **Write down one line for a new song about tonight.**\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Jules Moreau:** before your set.\n- **Skyler Monroe:** quietly.\n- **Jamie Ruiz:** a chance.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A microphone** (a prop), sunglasses and a set list.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nStage-ready: sequins, leather or both, and a lot of jewelry.";
STORY.dossiers["bailey"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The brand.** Three million followers, a perfect apartment, perfect outfits, perfect brunch. All of it is sponsored, borrowed or staged. The \"apartment\" is a rented set. You live in a studio with a roommate and a broken heater.\n\n**The dream.** You don\u0027t really want to be an influencer. You want to be a journalist, a real one, like Parker Lowell. You\u0027ve read everything Parker has written. Parker calls influencers \"content.\"\n\n**Tonight\u0027s deal.** The events company promised you $5,000 to post the gala. You haven\u0027t been paid yet.\n\n**The agent.** From the moment the FBI walked in, you\u0027ve been calling one of them \"the sexy FBI agent.\" You don\u0027t know his name, but you\u0027d know him anywhere, and you\u0027ve been keeping an eye on him all night. For research.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** to post the night, and maybe break a real story at last.\n- **Your plan:** post constantly, get every celebrity, and get Parker to notice you.\n- **How you play it:** bubbly and relentless, narrating everything, and sharper than anyone expects.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **At about 0:40 you notice the sexy FBI agent leave the main room.** He doesn\u0027t come back until after the alarm.\n- **At 0:45 you can\u0027t help yourself.** Post it right away: \"WHERE did the sexy FBI agent disappear to?? He was right here 5 min ago.\" (Your phone will post it for you if you forget.)\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| The sexy FBI agent | One of the agents. You don\u0027t know his name. You\u0027ve been watching him all night. |\n| Parker Lowell | Your hero. Thinks you\u0027re a joke. Prove otherwise. |\n| Dusty Featherstone | A podcaster competing for the room\u0027s attention. Rival, or collab? |\n| Gray Bishop | A politician who wants a selfie. Fine. |\n| Drew Kincaid | Owns the app you live on. Be nice. |\n| Remy Laurent | You posted Remy\u0027s engagement photos. |\n| Harper Quill | The event manager. Owes you $5,000. Harper\u0027s NightBank account fills up as the casino runs. Just saying. |\n| Skyler Monroe, Jet Okonkwo | Famously feuding. Get them in the same photo. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- Everything you\u0027ve seen tonight. You post it all anyway.\n- \"I don\u0027t miss anything. It\u0027s literally my job.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether your posts and photos are timestamped: yes, and you must show them.\n2. Asked who paid you to be here: the events company. (They haven\u0027t, yet.)\n\n**Keep secret:** the studio apartment, and how badly you want Parker\u0027s respect.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **Your perfect life is staged.**\n2. **You want to be a journalist,** and you\u0027re afraid you\u0027re only ever going to be \"content.\"\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Post at least five times tonight,** with photos.\n2. **Get Skyler and Jet in the same photo.**\n3. **At 0:45, post your question** about the sexy FBI agent.\n4. **Get Parker Lowell to take you seriously.**\n5. **Get paid your $5,000.**\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Parker Lowell:** your hero.\n- **The sexy FBI agent:** keep watching. If anyone asks which agent you mean, you can point him out in person.\n- **Skyler and Jet:** the photo.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **Your phone on a ring light,** and a sponsor\u0027s tote bag.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. You live on it. **NightBank**, for what little money you have tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too. Great content. Terrible odds.\n\n## Costume\n\nA borrowed designer outfit (with the tags tucked in), perfect hair and a ring light.";
STORY.dossiers["parker"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The reporter.** Ten years at the Harbor Ledger: corruption, fraud, cover-ups. You\u0027ve made enemies in every building in the city, Gray Bishop\u0027s office included.\n\n**The Ward Fake.** Six months ago you broke the story that FBI agent Dana Ward had announced the recovery of a stolen painting that turned out to be a forgery. It made your name. Then, quietly, you learned the truth: the forgery came from a master forger who had fooled three museums. Dana wasn\u0027t careless. Your story nearly destroyed an honest agent. You\u0027ve never corrected it.\n\n**Laid off.** Three months ago the Ledger cut half its newsroom, you included. Nobody knows yet. You\u0027re freelancing, and you need one big story to get back.\n\n**The tips.** Two anonymous messages, from two different senders:\n\n- Two weeks ago: \"Be at the Ashgrove gala. The Ashgrove Collection won\u0027t survive the night.\"\n- Three days ago: \"Ask about Hollis Grant, Lennox Blackwood, Indigo Hart, Wren Whitaker and Kendall Ashgrove-Moore. Every one of them wants Victor\u0027s art gone.\"\n\n**Harper.** The event manager, Harper Quill, has been feeding you details in exchange for a glowing write-up.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** the tips, and the story that gets your career back.\n- **Your plan:** watch everyone on the second tip\u0027s list, find out who sent each tip, and get the story first.\n- **How you play it:** polite and observant, always taking notes, and always asking one question too many.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **The tips were right.** A painting disappears, and people die. You have the story of your life, if you can work out who knew in advance.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Dana Ward | The agent you wrote about. You owe her an apology she doesn\u0027t know about. |\n| Harper Quill | Your inside source tonight. |\n| Gray Bishop | A politician who hates you. With good reason. |\n| Emerson Albright | Hiding something about a new exhibit. |\n| Blair Devereaux | A \"European heir\" who doesn\u0027t show up in any search. Interesting. |\n| Dusty Featherstone | A conspiracy podcaster. Embarrassing for everyone. |\n| Bailey Sparks | An influencer who keeps following you around. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Somebody knew this was going to happen. I have the messages to prove it.\"\n- Anything you can confirm. Nothing you can\u0027t.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether you received anonymous tips about tonight: yes, two. You must show them.\n2. Asked whether you still work for the Harbor Ledger: no.\n\n**Keep secret:** the layoff, and the truth about the Ward Fake.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You were laid off three months ago.** You need this story.\n2. **You know the Ward Fake story was unfair to Dana,** and you never corrected it.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Find out who sent each tip.** They didn\u0027t come from the same person. Compare the wording with anything written tonight. Someone selling data on NIGHTWIRE may know where they came from; Vivienne Roux can shop there.\n2. **Get the story first:** the theft, the murders and the truth.\n3. **Find out who Blair Devereaux really is.**\n4. **Decide whether to tell Dana the truth** about the Ward Fake.\n5. **Search the Harbor Ledger\u0027s archive** for anything about the Ashgroves. Your old login still works, for one search, before someone at the paper notices. Choose your search carefully. (Ask the host when you\u0027re ready to use it.)\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Dana Ward:** you owe her.\n- **Harper Quill:** your source.\n- **The five names on the second tip.**\n\n## You carry\n\n- **Printouts of both tips** (paper clues).\n- **A reporter\u0027s notebook, a recorder and a lanyard** reading PRESS.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your money tonight (a freelancer\u0027s budget). The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nSmart, practical and slightly underdressed for a gala: blazer, notebook, comfortable shoes.";
STORY.dossiers["hollis"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Ashgrove \u0026 Grant (1993 to 2015).** Victor was the smile. You were the money and the muscle. For twenty years you built a fortune together, and for twenty years you quietly **cooked the books**: moving money out through side deals Victor never understood. That\u0027s how you got rich, and how Victor, who owned the same company, slowly got poor. He never noticed.\n\n**2015.** Victor finally forced you out. He thought he\u0027d won.\n\n**Texas.** You went home, found oil, and built Grant Energy into an $18 billion company. You did it the way you always have: by suing people until they break, then buying what\u0027s left. You\u0027re famous for it. \"Sue \u0027em, ruin \u0027em, buy \u0027em.\"\n\n**Victor\u0027s debt.** A year ago your private investigators told you Victor was in trouble. Through Thorne Capital, a firm you set up and pay Cameron Thorne to front, you quietly bought up his loans. Every dollar Victor owes, he now owes to you. He doesn\u0027t know.\n\n**March 2001.** You remember the exact morning: March 14, 2001. Victor skipped a board meeting, came in white as a sheet, and didn\u0027t speak to anyone for a week. You never found out why.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** Victor invited you, so you\u0027d look guilty when his art disappears. You came anyway, because you\u0027re buying.\n- **Your plan:** take everything he owns, cheap: the collection, the company, the name. The more trouble he\u0027s in, the cheaper he gets. If he died, it would all get very cheap indeed.\n- **How you play it:** loud, generous and folksy, buying drinks for the whole room while you circle Victor like a buzzard.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **Between 0:40 and 0:50, you pull Remy into the east hall** and tell the truth: \"He\u0027s broke, darlin\u0027. He\u0027s been lying to you.\" Jamie sees you both leave.\n- **When Victor dies,** everyone remembers you\u0027re the man who profits most. You\u0027d better have an answer.\n\n## The money\n\nEighteen billion dollars doesn\u0027t fit in a wallet. You have **$20 million** on hand in NightBank tonight, more than anyone else in the room. You can free up another **$60 million** once tonight; it takes about an hour and a half on the game clock to clear. If a certain painting comes up for sale, you can bid yourself, or let Cameron bid for you and keep your name out of it.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Your old partner. A pretty face with no head for numbers. You own his debt. |\n| Remy Laurent | His fiancé(e). Remy deserves the truth, and Remy might make a useful witness in your lawsuit. |\n| Penn Calloway | Victor\u0027s money manager. Talks too much after two drinks. |\n| Quincy Abernathy | Victor\u0027s lawyer. Fought you in court for twelve years. Good at it. |\n| Cameron Thorne | Your front man. Collects Victor\u0027s debt in public; you paid a big check and an NDA to keep him quiet about who he works for. Text Cameron your orders. |\n| Gray Bishop | The councilmember. Everybody\u0027s for sale. |\n| Noor Haddad | An FBI analyst asking questions about Ashgrove \u0026 Grant. Careful. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"I made Victor Ashgrove. He\u0027ll tell you different.\"\n- \"I\u0027ve sued better men than him.\"\n- The story of March 2001, if anyone asks about Victor\u0027s past.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether you\u0027re suing Victor: yes.\n2. Asked where you were between 0:40 and 0:50: in the east hall, with Remy Laurent.\n\n**Keep secret:** that you own Victor\u0027s debt, your private investigators, and the cooked books.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You cooked Ashgrove \u0026 Grant\u0027s books for twenty years.** It\u0027s how you got rich and Victor got poor. If it comes out, your lawsuit is dead, and you might be too.\n2. **You secretly own all of Victor\u0027s debt.**\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Buy Victor\u0027s collection,** or at least make him an offer he can\u0027t refuse.\n2. **Tell Remy the truth** in Act I.\n3. **After Victor dies,** keep suspicion off you. You profit the most, and everyone knows it.\n4. **Keep the cooked books buried.** Watch Noor and Penn.\n5. **Find out what\u0027s really going on** with Victor\u0027s art. Something on these walls isn\u0027t right.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Victor:** make your offer.\n- **Remy:** the east hall.\n- **Penn Calloway:** a drink, and a few questions.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A Stetson, a glass of bourbon, and a business card** for Grant Energy.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone. \"If I wanted Victor dead, I\u0027d have bought the hospital.\"\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too. You like a table where the house wins.\n\n## Costume\n\nA white Stetson, a very expensive suit, boots, and a big belt buckle.";
STORY.dossiers["lennox"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Blackwood and Ashgrove.** Two collectors, two old family trees, and thirty years of outbidding each other. You despise Victor, and he returns the feeling.\n\n**The painting.** In 2005 the Vandermeer family sold *The Vanishing Hour* at auction. You had wanted it all your life. Victor outbid you by a single bid, then laughed in your face at the party afterward. You\u0027ve wanted it for twenty years.\n\n**The other collection.** Not everything you own came from an auction house. For decades you\u0027ve bought art that was stolen, looted or smuggled, no questions asked. You\u0027re one of the best-connected buyers of stolen art in the world, and nobody has ever proved it.\n\n**The rumor.** Two weeks ago your contacts told you a crew had been hired to hit the Ashgrove gala. You don\u0027t know who they are. You\u0027re sure **Hollis Grant** hired them, to ruin Victor before buying him out. You came to buy whatever they take.\n\n**The exhibit.** You pledged $12 million to Emerson\u0027s secret exhibit, just to beat Victor\u0027s $10 million, and you quietly lent it several pieces from your other collection.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** Victor invited you, which is strange after thirty years of hating each other. You came to buy.\n- **Your plan:** find the crew, make an offer, and finally take Victor\u0027s painting home.\n- **How you play it:** gracious, elegant and unhurried, watching everyone.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **After her arrest, the jewel thief tells the FBI you\u0027re here to buy a painting tonight.** Now the FBI thinks you\u0027re her partner, and they\u0027re watching you.\n\n## The money\n\nYou have **$12 million** on hand in NightBank tonight. You can free up another **$25 million** once tonight; it takes about an hour and a half on the game clock to clear. The FBI may freeze the account of anyone they have a warrant for. Move before they think of it.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Your rival for thirty years. He has your painting. |\n| Hollis Grant | You\u0027re sure Hollis hired the crew. Clever. |\n| Ainsley Vandermeer | The painting was Ainsley\u0027s family\u0027s, and Ainsley wants it back. A rival bidder. |\n| Drew Kincaid | A child with money. Another rival bidder. |\n| Emerson Albright | Took your $12 million. Knows where some of your loans came from. |\n| Vivienne Roux | A jewel thief who named you to the FBI. You\u0027ve never met her. |\n| Dana Ward | The FBI lead now watching you. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"Victor and I have always wanted the same things. He usually got them first.\"\n- \"I\u0027m a collector. I\u0027m always buying.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether you came tonight hoping to buy something: yes.\n2. Asked whether you know Vivienne Roux: no. You\u0027ve never met her.\n\n**Keep secret:** your other collection, and the pieces you lent Emerson.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You buy stolen art,** and you have for decades.\n2. **Some of Emerson\u0027s secret exhibit came from you.**\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Find the crew and buy Victor\u0027s painting,** whatever it costs.\n2. **Outbid Ainsley and Drew.**\n3. **After Vivienne names you, convince the FBI you\u0027re not her partner.**\n4. **Keep Emerson\u0027s exhibit, and your part in it, secret.**\n5. **Watch Victor lose.**\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Hollis Grant:** you think Hollis knows who the crew are.\n- **Emerson Albright:** keep your donation quiet.\n- **Whoever is selling.**\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A silver-tipped cane,** and a black business card with only a phone number on it.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. You never post. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nAll black, beautifully tailored, with one antique ring.";
STORY.dossiers["indigo"] = "## Backstory\n\n**Vale of Tears.** In 2019 you brought your best painting onto Peregrine Vale\u0027s show. Peregrine looked at it for four seconds and said: \"This isn\u0027t a painting, darling, it\u0027s a cry for help.\" The clip went viral. No gallery would touch you after that.\n\n**Victor\u0027s offer.** In 2023 Victor Ashgrove came to your studio. He said he needed exact copies of six paintings from his collection, \"conservation reproductions,\" so the originals could be cleaned and loaned out safely. One of them was a small oil, *Study for The Vanishing Hour*. He promised $200,000 and a solo show. You painted the best work of your life. He never paid you a cent, and the show never happened.\n\n**Your mark.** You always hide a tiny signature in your work: a dot of indigo blue and your initials, under the edge of the frame. Your copies have it too.\n\n**The invitation.** Then an invitation to his gala arrived. You came to look him in the eye.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** to confront Victor, and to see the collection.\n- **What you discover:** **one of the \"originals\" on the wall is yours.** Victor has been passing your copies off as the real thing, and selling the originals.\n- **How you play it:** guarded and sardonic, then furious.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **At 0:30 Peregrine Vale stands in front of your copy and declares it \"genuine and priceless.\"** The same critic who destroyed your career just called your work a masterpiece.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Cheated you out of $200,000 and a show, and hung your work as his own. |\n| Peregrine Vale | Called your work \"a cry for help\" on television. Tonight called it priceless. |\n| Dr. Ari Castellane | The curator. If anyone can help prove which paintings are yours, it\u0027s Ari. |\n| Drew Kincaid | A young billionaire who paid Victor $4 million for *Study for The Vanishing Hour*, thinking it was the original. It isn\u0027t. It\u0027s one of your six copies, and your mark proves it. |\n| Parker Lowell | A journalist. A story like yours could make Parker\u0027s career, and restart yours. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"I\u0027m a painter. Peregrine Vale ended my career in four seconds.\"\n- \"Victor Ashgrove owes me $200,000.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether Victor ever hired you: yes, in 2023, to paint six reproductions.\n2. Asked whether any painting in this room is yours: yes. You must say which one.\n\n**Keep secret:** that you painted the copies, until you decide to tell.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You painted six copies for Victor,** and one of them is hanging on the wall as an original.\n2. **You hid your mark in every one.**\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Confront Victor** about the money and the show.\n2. **Prove which paintings are yours** without being branded a forger.\n3. **Find out where the real originals went.**\n4. **Get Peregrine Vale to admit,** on Bebbit or to the room, that your work is good.\n5. **Get paid, or get the credit.**\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Victor Ashgrove:** the money.\n- **Dr. Ari Castellane:** the proof.\n- **Peregrine Vale:** the admission.\n- **Drew Kincaid:** he deserves to know what he bought.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A small sketchbook with studies of all six paintings** (a paper clue).\n- **Paint under your fingernails.**\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for what little money you have tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nThrift-store formal with paint-stained shoes, and something indigo.";
STORY.dossiers["wren"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The job.** You joined Ashgrove \u0026 Grant in 2016, right out of school, checking that the company followed the rules. In 2017 you even handled the donation of the company\u0027s old office papers to the museum archive: forty boxes, going back to 1993.\n\n**2019.** You noticed something you weren\u0027t supposed to: design files from Meridian Optics, a military contractor the company had just bought, being sent to a company in Cyprus called Larkspur Holdings. Military designs don\u0027t go to Cyprus.\n\n**2020.** You reported it to the regulators. They dismissed it. Victor fired you and sued you. No company will hire you now. You drive deliveries at night.\n\n**The FBI.** What nobody knows: after the regulators failed, you went to the FBI. An analyst named **Noor Haddad** believed you. You\u0027ve been Noor\u0027s secret source for two years.\n\n**The invitation.** Victor invited you tonight, probably so the bitter ex-employee takes the blame for something. You came because Noor asked you to.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** Noor needs you in the building.\n- **Your plan:** keep your head down, check in with Noor without anyone noticing, and watch Victor.\n- **How you play it:** polite, nervous and out of place, and braver than anyone in the room.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **When Victor dies, Noor\u0027s case is in danger.** You know exactly where Victor\u0027s old papers are: in the museum archive, box numbers and all. The boxes are locked. Dr. Ari Castellane, the curator, has the key.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Noor Haddad | Your FBI contact. Nobody can know. |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Fired you and sued you for telling the truth. |\n| Penn Calloway | Victor\u0027s money manager. Penn must know where the Cyprus money went. |\n| Hollis Grant | Left the company before your time. You\u0027ve heard the stories. |\n| Parker Lowell | A journalist who could tell your story. Not yet: it would wreck Noor\u0027s case. |\n| Dr. Ari Castellane | The curator, who keeps the archive keys. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"I told the truth about Ashgrove \u0026 Grant, and it cost me everything.\"\n- \"The company\u0027s old papers are in the museum archive. I packed them myself.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether you reported Ashgrove \u0026 Grant to regulators: yes, in 2020.\n2. Asked whether you\u0027ve talked to the FBI before tonight: yes. You may refuse to say who.\n\n**Keep secret:** that Noor is your contact, and what you saw in 2019, until Noor says it\u0027s safe.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You\u0027re the FBI\u0027s secret source** on LARKSPUR.\n2. **You\u0027ve lost everything,** and you\u0027ve never told your family why.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Check in with Noor** without anyone seeing.\n2. **After Victor dies, help Noor save the case:** tell Noor which archive box holds Victor\u0027s 2001 papers, and help get the key from Ari.\n3. **Find out where the Cyprus money went.** Penn knows.\n4. **Don\u0027t let Parker turn you into a story.** Not yet.\n5. **Hear someone, anyone, say you were right.**\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Noor Haddad:** quietly.\n- **Penn Calloway:** the money.\n- **Dr. Ari Castellane:** the archive key.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A worn folder** with your 2020 regulator complaint (a paper clue).\n- **A delivery-app jacket** you keep forgetting to take off.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for the little money you have tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too. You can\u0027t afford it.\n\n## Costume\n\nA rented suit that doesn\u0027t quite fit, and the jacket.";
STORY.dossiers["kendall"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The marriage.** You married Victor in 1998. Your family knew all the right people; Victor had the name. For a while it was good.\n\n**Spring 2001.** You wanted children. You\u0027d talked about it for years. Then, in the spring of 2001, Victor changed. He came home one night and said, flatly: \"I\u0027ll never be a father. Don\u0027t ask me again.\" He never explained. You spent eight more years hoping he\u0027d change his mind. He didn\u0027t. In 2009 you left.\n\n**The name.** You kept \"Ashgrove.\" It opens doors, and you earned it.\n\n**Hollis.** You always wondered about Hollis. The year Victor had to sell your country house, Hollis bought a ranch. Funny timing.\n\n**The invitation.** Victor invited you tonight, most likely so his bitter ex can take the blame for something. You came to see Remy for yourself.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** curiosity, and pride.\n- **Your plan:** meet Remy, warn Remy if you can, and remind Victor you\u0027re doing just fine.\n- **How you play it:** polished, funny, a little cruel, and very good at reading a room.\n\n## What happens\n\n- **At about 1:30, your phone will nudge you** to tell someone what Victor said to you in 2001.\n- **If the truth about 2001 comes out,** you\u0027ll learn that Victor had a son that year, with another woman, while he was married to you. That\u0027s why he swore he\u0027d never be a father. You gave up eight years hoping he\u0027d change his mind, and he already had a child. You\u0027ll be furious, and you\u0027re allowed to show it.\n\n## The money\n\nYou have **$2 million** on hand in NightBank tonight. Moore \u0026 Partners can free up another **$4 million** once tonight; it takes about an hour and a half on the game clock to clear.\n\n## Relationships\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| Victor Ashgrove | Your ex. Swore he\u0027d never be a father. You still don\u0027t know why. |\n| Remy Laurent | Victor\u0027s new fiancé(e). Hates that you kept the name. You almost feel sorry for Remy. |\n| Quincy Abernathy | Victor\u0027s lawyer in the divorce. Very polite. Very effective. |\n| Hollis Grant | Victor\u0027s old partner. Always seemed to have more money than he should. |\n| Marlowe Pike | Victor\u0027s assistant since 2000. You\u0027ve always thought Marlowe knows something about 2001. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- \"I was married to Victor for eleven years. Ask me anything.\"\n- \"Victor never wanted children.\"\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. Asked whether Victor ever wanted children: \"He told me he\u0027d never be a father.\"\n2. Asked when he first said it: \"The spring of 2001.\"\n\n**Keep secret:** how much you wanted children, and how much it still hurts.\n\n## Your secrets\n\n1. **You wanted children,** and Victor\u0027s refusal ended your marriage.\n2. **You still care about him, a little.** You\u0027d never admit it.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Meet Remy,** and decide whether to warn Remy about Victor.\n2. **Find out why Victor changed in 2001.**\n3. **Make sure Victor sees you\u0027re thriving** without him.\n4. **Find out whether Hollis cheated Victor** all those years.\n5. **If the truth about 2001 comes out,** decide what to do with it.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Remy Laurent:** the warning.\n- **Marlowe Pike:** what happened in 2001?\n- **Hollis Grant:** that ranch.\n\n## You carry\n\n- **A business card** for Moore \u0026 Partners, and a silver compact you check constantly.\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too.\n\n## Costume\n\nSharp, expensive and a little intimidating: the best-dressed ex in the room.";
STORY.dossiers["dusty"] = "## Backstory\n\n**The show.** *Wake Up, America* is political true crime with a conspiracy twist. Every episode, you lean into the microphone, furrow your brow, and say: \"I\u0027m just asking questions.\" You have over a million followers. About 900,000 of them are bots you bought.\n\n**The invitation.** Three weeks ago, a gold-edged invitation to the Ashgrove gala arrived at your apartment. Your name is on the guest list. You don\u0027t know Victor Ashgrove. You don\u0027t know anyone at this party. You have no idea who put you there, and you\u0027ve decided it\u0027s because you\u0027re onto something.\n\n**Your mission.** Get in with the FBI. Crack the case before they do. Record everything for the show.\n\n## Tonight\n\n- **Why you\u0027re here:** honestly, nobody knows. Including you.\n- **Your plan:** find a conspiracy, record it, and get an FBI agent to call you \"a valuable asset.\"\n- **How you play it:** wacky, confident and unstoppable. You\u0027re never obnoxious, just always there. You notice things, and you make problems.\n\n## What you\u0027ve done tonight (before the game even starts)\n\n- **You wandered into the vault stairwell** before the doors opened, \"by accident.\" Security walked you out.\n- **You asked Agent Rowan Hale for an autograph.** He signed it. You have it.\n- **You found a cool little gadget** on the floor by the bar. You have no idea what it is. It\u0027s yours now.\n- **You\u0027ve taken 400 photos** for the show. You haven\u0027t looked through them.\n\n## Your theory\n\nBefore anyone dies, your theory is that something big is going down tonight and the elites don\u0027t want you to know. After Victor dies: **\"He faked his own death, folks. Obviously.\"** Commit to it.\n\n## Relationships\n\nYou don\u0027t know anyone. That has never stopped you.\n\n| Who | What you think of them |\n| --- | --- |\n| The FBI agents | Your future colleagues. They just don\u0027t know it yet. |\n| Parker Lowell | A \"mainstream media\" journalist. Your nemesis, as of tonight. |\n| Bailey Sparks | An influencer. Competition for the room\u0027s attention. Or a collab? |\n| Rowan Hale | The agent who signed your autograph. Nice guy. Very handsome. |\n\n## What you know\n\n**Share freely:**\n\n- Every theory you have, out loud, to anyone.\n- \"I\u0027ve got four hundred photos, and the truth is in one of them.\"\n\n**Your photos (a clue):** somewhere in your 400 photos is one you didn\u0027t notice: **Hollis Grant and Remy Laurent in the east hall, with a clock behind them reading 7:45** (0:45 on the game clock). If someone looks through your photos, it shows exactly where those two were while Charlie was on the vault stairs.\n\n**Sworn facts** (if an FBI agent asks you directly, you must tell the truth):\n\n1. You don\u0027t know anyone at this party.\n2. If an agent asks to see your photos, you must show them.\n\n**Keep secret:** the bots.\n\n## Your secret\n\n**Your million followers are 90 percent fake.** You bought them. If anyone finds out, your career is over.\n\n## Goals tonight\n\n1. **Get in with the FBI.** Get at least one agent to accept a \"tip\" from you.\n2. **Find out who put you on the guest list.**\n3. **Record the night for the show.** Post at least three times on Bebbit with a theory.\n4. **After Victor dies:** convince at least three people he faked his own death.\n5. **Protect your follower count.** Nobody can find out about the bots.\n6. **Show off your gadget** to everyone all night, but never long enough for anyone to see what it is.\n\n## Who to find\n\n- **Any FBI agent:** your tips.\n- **Parker Lowell:** your rival.\n- **Whoever looks like they invited you.**\n\n## You carry\n\n- **Your phone, held up and recording, all night.**\n- **Rowan\u0027s autograph** on a cocktail napkin, and the cool little gadget.\n- **Printouts or a slideshow of your photos** (the host provides them, with the clue photo hidden among them).\n\n## Lying\n\nYou may lie about anything except your two sworn facts. You didn\u0027t kill anyone. You think.\n\n## Your apps\n\n**Bebbit**, like everyone. Post often. Post loudly. **NightBank**, for your money tonight. The gala\u0027s charity casino is in there too. Is it rigged? You\u0027re just asking questions.\n\n## Costume\n\nA blazer one size too small, an open collar, a lapel microphone, and a phone on a selfie grip.";
